-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 16, sexual offences: voyeurism, intimate
-- images, sexual exposure, child abuse material and abusive material, with the
-- interpretation section (s 377C) they all read, the defences (ss 377BM,
-- 377BN) and the extraterritorial section (s 377BO): the sections the first
-- pass left deferred, ss 377BB to 377BO and 377C.
-- Completion pass of 2026-11-04 by one Sonnet 5.5 agent.
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO "Current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026" (a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text),
-- registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt lines 9062-10062.
--
-- What a reader must know before reading:
--
-- * Each offence has the contract's four items (facts record, defining
--   predicate, `offence under s N`, `charge under s N`). The ladders are
--   BOOLEAN: FALSE there means "the elements are not made out on the facts
--   stated", not "the text says no". The definitions (s 377C and the
--   "ways ... may include" subsections), the presumptions, the defences and
--   the rules of reading ("it is not necessary to prove ...") are functions
--   that return MAYBE BOOLEAN or a named constructor: JUST FALSE only where
--   the text says no in its own words, NOTHING (or a "not covered"
--   constructor) everywhere else, each branch marked FALSE-kind or
--   NOTHING-kind in a comment.
-- * A defence here is a function over the facts it needs (the accused's
--   proof, the purposes, the conditions); the offences' ladders do not call
--   it: whether a defence is raised is for the court after the elements.
-- * Where a leaf is set from a definition (child abuse material, private
--   act, intimate image), the leaf's @desc names the function.
-- * "Electronic record" is the Electronic Transactions Act 2010's meaning,
--   and "sexual offence" in s 335A is the Criminal Procedure Code 2010's: not
--   in the sources, so inputs.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`

§ `Chapter 16 - ss 377BB-377BO and 377C, completed`


§§ `s 377C - interpretation of sections 375 to 377BO (sexual offences)`

-- src:9907 | Interpretation of sections 375 to 377BO (sexual offences)
-- src:9909 | 377C.—(1) In this section and in sections 375 to 377BO —
-- src:9911 | “buttocks”, in relation to a person, includes the anal region of the person;
-- src:9915 | “child abuse material” means material that depicts an image of any of the
-- src:9918 | following (whether or not any child was involved in the production of the
-- src:9919 | material):
-- src:9921 | (a) a person who is, or who appears to a reasonable observer to be, or
-- src:9922 | who is implied to be, below 16 years of age —
-- src:9923 | (i) as a victim of torture, cruelty or physical abuse (whether or
-- src:9924 | not the torture, cruelty or abuse is sexual);
-- src:9926 | (ii) as a victim of sexual abuse;
-- src:9928 | (iii) engaged in, or apparently engaging in, a sexual pose or
-- src:9929 | sexual activity (whether or not in the presence of another
-- src:9930 | person); or
-- src:9932 | (iv) in the presence of another person who is engaged in, or
-- src:9933 | apparently engaged in a sexual pose or sexual activity;
-- src:9935 | (b) the genital region or buttocks (whether exposed or covered) of a
-- src:9936 | person who is, or who appears to a reasonable observer to be, or who
-- src:9937 | is implied to be, a person below 16 years of age, where the depiction
-- src:9938 | is sexual and in circumstances (whether or not apparent from the
-- src:9939 | depiction) which reasonable persons would regard as being offensive;
-- src:9943 | (c) the breasts (whether exposed or covered) of a person who is, or who
-- src:9944 | appears to a reasonable observer to be, or who is implied to be, a
-- src:9945 | female below 16 years of age, where the depiction is sexual and in
-- src:9946 | circumstances (whether or not apparent from the depiction) which
-- src:9947 | reasonable persons would regard as being offensive;
-- src:9952 | “distribute” includes any of the following conduct, whether done in person,
-- src:9953 | electronically, digitally or in any other way:
-- src:9955 | (a) send, publish, supply, show, exhibit, transmit or communicate to
-- src:9956 | another person;
-- src:9958 | (b) make available for viewing or access by another person;
-- src:9960 | “image” means a still, moving, recorded or unrecorded image and includes an
-- src:9961 | image produced by any means and, where the context requires, a
-- src:9962 | three-dimensional image;
-- src:9964 | “image”, in relation to a person, means —
-- src:9967 | (a) an image of a human being who is not fictional or imaginary (whether
-- src:9968 | identifiable or not); or
-- src:9970 | (b) an image of a fictional or imaginary human being that so closely
-- src:9971 | resembles an image of a human being who is not fictional or
-- src:9972 | imaginary (whether identifiable or not) as to make it difficult for an
-- src:9973 | ordinary person to distinguish the firstmentioned image from an
-- src:9974 | image of a human being who is not fictional or imaginary;
-- src:9978 | “material” means —
-- src:9980 | (a) any film, photograph, printed matter or computer game depicting an
-- src:9981 | image;
-- src:9983 | (b) any electronic record depicting an image; or
-- src:9985 | (c) any other thing of any kind depicting an image;
-- src:9987 | “structure” includes a tent, vehicle or vessel or other temporary or movable
-- src:9988 | structure;
-- src:9990 | “touching” includes touching —
-- src:9992 | (a) with any part of the body;
-- src:9994 | (b) with anything else; or
-- src:9996 | (c) through anything,
-- src:9998 | and includes penetration of the vagina or anus, as the case may be, with a part
-- src:9999 | of the body or anything else and penetration of the mouth with the penis;
-- src:10001 | “vagina” includes vulva.
-- src:10006 | (2) For the purposes of the definition of “distribute” in subsection (1), a person is
-- src:10007 | treated as having distributed an image or recording whether or not another person views
-- src:10008 | or gains access to the image.
-- src:10012 | (3) In sections 375 to 377BO —
-- src:10014 | (a) penetration is a continuing act from entry to withdrawal;
-- src:10016 | (b) a reference to a part of the body includes a reference to a part which is
-- src:10017 | surgically constructed (in particular, through a sex reassignment
-- src:10018 | procedure);
-- src:10021 | (c) for the purposes of identifying the sex of a person —
-- src:10022 | (i) the sex of a person as stated in that person’s identity card issued
-- src:10023 | under the National Registration Act 1965 at the time the sexual
-- src:10024 | activity took place is prima facie evidence of the sex of that
-- src:10025 | person; and
-- src:10027 | (ii) a person who has undergone a sex reassignment procedure is
-- src:10028 | identified as being of the sex to which that person has been
-- src:10029 | reassigned;
-- src:10031 | (d) penetration, touching, communication or other activity is “sexual” if —
-- src:10032 | (i) because of its nature it is sexual, whatever its circumstances or
-- src:10033 | any person’s purpose in relation to it may be; or
-- src:10035 | (ii) because of its nature it may be sexual and because of its
-- src:10036 | circumstances or the purpose of any person in relation to it (or
-- src:10037 | both) it is sexual;
-- src:10039 | (e) references to observation (however expressed) are to observation whether
-- src:10040 | direct or by looking at an image;
-- src:10042 | (f) a person is doing a private act if under circumstances in which the person
-- src:10043 | has a reasonable expectation of privacy, the person —
-- src:10044 | (i) is in a state where the person’s genital region, buttocks or
-- src:10045 | breasts (if the person is a female) are exposed or covered only in
-- src:10046 | underwear;
-- src:10050 | (ii) is using a toilet, showering or bathing; or
-- src:10052 | (iii) is doing a sexual act that is not of a kind ordinarily done in
-- src:10053 | public.
-- src:10055 | Illustration
-- src:10057 | A is showering in an open-concept shower cubicle at the changing
-- src:10058 | room of a swimming pool and cannot reasonably expect not to be casually
-- src:10059 | observed. However, A has a reasonable expectation that A will not be
-- src:10060 | surreptitiously recorded by a video camera.
-- Definitions and rules of reading, as functions: MAYBE BOOLEAN, JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words
-- ("means", "if", flat negatives), NOTHING where it says "includes", "may include", or is limited by its own wording.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C (src:9907-10060)
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(1) "buttocks" (src:9911-9911)
@export Whether a region is within "buttocks" in relation to a person, section 377C(1) of the Penal Code 1871: it includes the anal region
GIVEN `it is the anal region of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the region the anal region of the person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(1) the region is within "buttocks"` MEANS
    IF `it is the anal region of the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "\"buttocks\", in relation to a person, includes the anal region of the person"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(1) "child abuse material" (src:9915-9947)
@export Whether material is "child abuse material" within section 377C(1) of the Penal Code 1871: material that depicts an image of a person who is, or appears to a reasonable observer to be, or is implied to be, below 16 years of age, as a victim of abuse, in a sexual pose or activity, or in the presence of another in one; or the sexual and offensive depiction of the genital region, buttocks or (if female) breasts of such a person
GIVEN `it is material within the definition in section 377C(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing "material" - see `s 377C(1) the thing is material`?
      `the person depicted is, or appears to a reasonable observer to be, or is implied to be, below 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person depicted below 16 years of age, or does the person appear to a reasonable observer to be, or is the person implied to be, below 16?
      `any child was involved in the production of the material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was any child involved in the production of the material? NOT relevant: the definition applies "whether or not any child was involved"
      `the image is of the person as a victim of torture, cruelty or physical abuse (whether or not the torture, cruelty or abuse is sexual)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image of the person as a victim of torture, cruelty or physical abuse, whether or not sexual? (s 377C(1) paragraph (a)(i))
      `the image is of the person as a victim of sexual abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image of the person as a victim of sexual abuse? (paragraph (a)(ii))
      `the image is of the person engaged in, or apparently engaging in, a sexual pose or sexual activity (whether or not in the presence of another person)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image of the person engaged in, or apparently engaging in, a sexual pose or sexual activity, whether or not in the presence of another person? (paragraph (a)(iii))
      `the image is of the person in the presence of another person who is engaged in, or apparently engaged in, a sexual pose or sexual activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image of the person in the presence of another person who is engaged in, or apparently engaged in, a sexual pose or sexual activity? (paragraph (a)(iv))
      `the image is of the genital region or buttocks (whether exposed or covered) of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image of the genital region or buttocks (whether exposed or covered) of the person? (paragraph (b))
      `the image is of the breasts (whether exposed or covered) of a female` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image of the breasts (whether exposed or covered) of a female? (paragraph (c))
      `the depiction is sexual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the depiction sexual? See `s 377C(3)(d) the conduct is sexual`
      `reasonable persons would regard the circumstances as offensive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances (whether or not apparent from the depiction) such that reasonable persons would regard them as offensive?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(1) the material is child abuse material` MEANS
    IF `it is material within the definition in section 377C(1)` AND `the person depicted is, or appears to a reasonable observer to be, or is implied to be, below 16 years of age` AND (`the image is of the person as a victim of torture, cruelty or physical abuse (whether or not the torture, cruelty or abuse is sexual)` OR `the image is of the person as a victim of sexual abuse` OR `the image is of the person engaged in, or apparently engaging in, a sexual pose or sexual activity (whether or not in the presence of another person)` OR `the image is of the person in the presence of another person who is engaged in, or apparently engaged in, a sexual pose or sexual activity` OR (`the image is of the genital region or buttocks (whether exposed or covered) of the person` AND `the depiction is sexual` AND `reasonable persons would regard the circumstances as offensive`) OR (`the image is of the breasts (whether exposed or covered) of a female` AND `the depiction is sexual` AND `reasonable persons would regard the circumstances as offensive`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"child abuse material\" means material that depicts an image of any of the following (whether or not any child was involved in the production of the material)"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(1) "distribute" (src:9952-9958)
@export Whether conduct is "distribute" within section 377C(1) of the Penal Code 1871: it includes sending, publishing, supplying, showing, exhibiting, transmitting or communicating to another person, and making available for viewing or access by another person
GIVEN `the conduct is to send, publish, supply, show, exhibit, transmit or communicate to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conduct to send, publish, supply, show, exhibit, transmit or communicate to another person, in person, electronically, digitally or in any other way?
      `the conduct is to make available for viewing or access by another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conduct to make available for viewing or access by another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(1) the conduct is distributing` MEANS
    IF `the conduct is to send, publish, supply, show, exhibit, transmit or communicate to another person` OR `the conduct is to make available for viewing or access by another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "\"distribute\" includes any of the following conduct"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(2) (src:10006-10008)
@export Whether, under section 377C(2) of the Penal Code 1871, a person is treated as having distributed an image or recording only if another person views or gains access to it: no, whether or not
GIVEN `another person views or gains access to the image` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another person view or gain access to the image or recording? The answer changes nothing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(2) distributing requires that another person views or gains access to the image` MEANS
    JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is treated as having distributed an image or recording whether or not another person views or gains access to the image"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(1) "image" (src:9960-9962)
@export Whether a thing is an "image" within section 377C(1) of the Penal Code 1871: a still, moving, recorded or unrecorded image, and any image produced by any means, and where the context requires, a three-dimensional image
GIVEN `it is a still, moving, recorded or unrecorded image` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a still, moving, recorded or unrecorded image?
      `it is an image produced by any means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an image produced by any means?
      `it is a three-dimensional image and the context requires it to count` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a three-dimensional image, where the context requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(1) the thing is an image` MEANS
    IF `it is a still, moving, recorded or unrecorded image` OR `it is an image produced by any means` OR `it is a three-dimensional image and the context requires it to count`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "\"image\" means a still, moving, recorded or unrecorded image and includes an image produced by any means and, where the context requires, a three-dimensional image"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(1) "image", in relation to a person (src:9964-9974)
@export Whether an image is an "image" in relation to a person, section 377C(1) of the Penal Code 1871: an image of a human being who is not fictional or imaginary, or of a fictional or imaginary human being so closely resembling one that an ordinary person would find it difficult to tell the two apart
GIVEN `it is an image of a human being who is not fictional or imaginary (whether identifiable or not)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an image of a human being who is not fictional or imaginary, whether identifiable or not?
      `it is an image of a fictional or imaginary human being that so closely resembles an image of a human being who is not fictional or imaginary as to make it difficult for an ordinary person to distinguish the two` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an image of a fictional or imaginary human being that so closely resembles an image of a real human being (identifiable or not) that an ordinary person would find it difficult to distinguish the two?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(1) the image is an image in relation to a person` MEANS
    IF `it is an image of a human being who is not fictional or imaginary (whether identifiable or not)` OR `it is an image of a fictional or imaginary human being that so closely resembles an image of a human being who is not fictional or imaginary as to make it difficult for an ordinary person to distinguish the two`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"image\", in relation to a person, means (a) an image of a human being who is not fictional or imaginary ...; or (b) an image of a fictional or imaginary human being that so closely resembles ..."

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(1) "material" (src:9978-9985)
@export Whether a thing is "material" within section 377C(1) of the Penal Code 1871: a film, photograph, printed matter or computer game depicting an image, an electronic record depicting an image, or any other thing of any kind depicting an image
GIVEN `it is a film, photograph, printed matter or computer game depicting an image` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a film, photograph, printed matter or computer game depicting an image?
      `it is an electronic record depicting an image` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an electronic record depicting an image? "Electronic record" has the meaning of the Electronic Transactions Act 2010 (s 29B)
      `it is any other thing of any kind depicting an image` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it any other thing of any kind depicting an image?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(1) the thing is material` MEANS
    IF `it is a film, photograph, printed matter or computer game depicting an image` OR `it is an electronic record depicting an image` OR `it is any other thing of any kind depicting an image`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"material\" means (a) any film, photograph, printed matter or computer game depicting an image; (b) any electronic record depicting an image; or (c) any other thing of any kind depicting an image"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(1) "structure" (src:9987-9988)
@export Whether a thing is a "structure" within section 377C(1) of the Penal Code 1871: it includes a tent, vehicle or vessel or other temporary or movable structure
GIVEN `it is a tent, vehicle or vessel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a tent, vehicle or vessel?
      `it is another temporary or movable structure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it another temporary or movable structure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(1) the thing is a structure` MEANS
    IF `it is a tent, vehicle or vessel` OR `it is another temporary or movable structure`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "\"structure\" includes a tent, vehicle or vessel or other temporary or movable structure"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(1) "touching" (src:9990-9999)
@export Whether an act is "touching" within section 377C(1) of the Penal Code 1871: it includes touching with any part of the body, with anything else, or through anything, and penetration of the vagina or anus with a part of the body or anything else and of the mouth with the penis
GIVEN `it is touching with any part of the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it touching with any part of the body?
      `it is touching with anything else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it touching with anything else?
      `it is touching through anything` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it touching through anything?
      `it is penetration of the vagina or anus with a part of the body or anything else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it penetration of the vagina or anus, as the case may be, with a part of the body or anything else?
      `it is penetration of the mouth with the penis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it penetration of the mouth with the penis?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(1) the act is touching` MEANS
    IF `it is touching with any part of the body` OR `it is touching with anything else` OR `it is touching through anything` OR `it is penetration of the vagina or anus with a part of the body or anything else` OR `it is penetration of the mouth with the penis`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "\"touching\" includes touching (a) with any part of the body; (b) with anything else; or (c) through anything, and includes penetration of the vagina or anus ... and penetration of the mouth with the penis"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(1) "vagina" (src:10001-10001)
@export Whether a part is within "vagina" in section 377C(1) of the Penal Code 1871: it includes the vulva
GIVEN `it is the vulva` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the part the vulva?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(1) the part is within "vagina"` MEANS
    IF `it is the vulva`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "\"vagina\" includes vulva"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(3)(a) (src:10014-10014)
@export Whether penetration is continuing at a point of time, section 377C(3)(a) of the Penal Code 1871: it is a continuing act from entry to withdrawal
GIVEN `entry has taken place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has entry taken place?
      `withdrawal has taken place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has withdrawal taken place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(3)(a) the penetration is continuing` MEANS
    IF `entry has taken place` AND NOT (`withdrawal has taken place`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says the act continues from entry to withdrawal; it does not say what the law is before entry or after withdrawal

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(3)(b) (src:10016-10018)
@export Whether a part is "a part of the body" in sections 375 to 377BO of the Penal Code 1871, section 377C(3)(b): it includes a part surgically constructed, in particular through a sex reassignment procedure
GIVEN `it is a part which is surgically constructed (in particular, through a sex reassignment procedure)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the part surgically constructed, in particular through a sex reassignment procedure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(3)(b) the part is a part of the body` MEANS
    IF `it is a part which is surgically constructed (in particular, through a sex reassignment procedure)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference to a part of the body includes a reference to a part which is surgically constructed"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(3)(d) (src:10031-10037)
@export Whether penetration, touching, communication or other activity is "sexual" within section 377C(3)(d) of the Penal Code 1871: sexual by its nature whatever the circumstances or purpose, or of a nature that may be sexual and sexual because of the circumstances or the purpose of any person, or both
GIVEN `because of its nature it is sexual, whatever its circumstances or any person's purpose in relation to it may be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it, because of its nature, sexual, whatever its circumstances or any person's purpose in relation to it may be? (s 377C(3)(d)(i))
      `because of its nature it may be sexual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it, because of its nature, something that may be sexual? (s 377C(3)(d)(ii))
      `because of its circumstances or the purpose of any person in relation to it (or both) it is sexual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Because of its circumstances or the purpose of any person in relation to it (or both), is it sexual? (s 377C(3)(d)(ii))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(3)(d) the conduct is sexual` MEANS
    IF `because of its nature it is sexual, whatever its circumstances or any person's purpose in relation to it may be` OR (`because of its nature it may be sexual` AND `because of its circumstances or the purpose of any person in relation to it (or both) it is sexual`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "penetration, touching, communication or other activity is \"sexual\" if (i) ...; or (ii) ..." (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(3)(e) (src:10039-10040)
@export Whether an observation is "observation" in sections 375 to 377BO of the Penal Code 1871, section 377C(3)(e): observation whether direct or by looking at an image
GIVEN `the observation is direct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the observation direct?
      `the observation is by looking at an image` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the observation by looking at an image?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(3)(e) the observation is observation within the sections` MEANS
    IF `the observation is direct` OR `the observation is by looking at an image`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names two kinds of observation; it does not say that observation in any other way is not observation

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(3)(f) (src:10042-10053)
@export Whether a person is "doing a private act" within section 377C(3)(f) of the Penal Code 1871: in circumstances where the person has a reasonable expectation of privacy, the person is in a state of undress or covered only in underwear, is using a toilet, showering or bathing, or is doing a sexual act not ordinarily done in public
GIVEN `the person has a reasonable expectation of privacy in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have a reasonable expectation of privacy in the circumstances - against what was done? See the Illustration: in an open-concept shower the person cannot expect not to be casually observed, but can expect not to be surreptitiously recorded by a video camera
      `the person is in a state where the person's genital region, buttocks or breasts (if the person is a female) are exposed or covered only in underwear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person in a state where the person's genital region, buttocks or breasts (if the person is a female) are exposed or covered only in underwear? (s 377C(3)(f)(i))
      `the person is using a toilet, showering or bathing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person using a toilet, showering or bathing? (s 377C(3)(f)(ii))
      `the person is doing a sexual act that is not of a kind ordinarily done in public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person doing a sexual act that is not of a kind ordinarily done in public? (s 377C(3)(f)(iii))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(3)(f) the person is doing a private act` MEANS
    IF `the person has a reasonable expectation of privacy in the circumstances` AND (`the person is in a state where the person's genital region, buttocks or breasts (if the person is a female) are exposed or covered only in underwear` OR `the person is using a toilet, showering or bathing` OR `the person is doing a sexual act that is not of a kind ordinarily done in public`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is doing a private act if under circumstances in which the person has a reasonable expectation of privacy, the person (i) ...; (ii) ...; or (iii) ..." (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)

-- 377C(3)(c): "for the purposes of identifying the sex of a person (i) the sex of a person as
-- stated in that person's identity card ... at the time the sexual activity took place is prima
-- facie evidence of the sex of that person; and (ii) a person who has undergone a sex
-- reassignment procedure is identified as being of the sex to which that person has been reassigned"
DECLARE `Sex of a person` IS ONE OF
    `the male sex`
    `the female sex`

DECLARE `Identified sex` HAS
    sex IS A `Sex of a person` @desc The sex the person is identified as
    `prima facie evidence only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE where the identification rests only on the identity card, which is prima facie evidence and may be rebutted; FALSE where the person has been reassigned and "is identified as" the reassigned sex

GIVEN s IS A `Sex of a person`
GIVETH AN `Identified sex`
`identified as the reassigned sex` s MEANS `Identified sex` WITH
    sex IS s
    `prima facie evidence only` IS FALSE

GIVEN s IS A `Sex of a person`
GIVETH AN `Identified sex`
`identified from the identity card` s MEANS `Identified sex` WITH
    sex IS s
    `prima facie evidence only` IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377C(3)(c) (src:10021-10029)
@export Which sex a person is identified as for sections 375 to 377BO of the Penal Code 1871, section 377C(3)(c): a person who has undergone a sex reassignment procedure is identified as the sex reassigned to; otherwise the sex stated in the person's identity card at the time is prima facie evidence of it
GIVEN `the person has undergone a sex reassignment procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person undergone a sex reassignment procedure?
      `the sex to which the person has been reassigned` IS A `Sex of a person` @desc The sex to which the person has been reassigned (ignored if there was no reassignment)
      `the person has an identity card issued under the National Registration Act 1965 stating a sex at the time the sexual activity took place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have such an identity card?
      `the sex stated in the identity card` IS A `Sex of a person` @desc The sex the identity card states (ignored if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Identified sex`
`s 377C(3)(c) the sex of the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has undergone a sex reassignment procedure`
        THEN JUST (`identified as the reassigned sex` `the sex to which the person has been reassigned`)
        IF `the person has an identity card issued under the National Registration Act 1965 stating a sex at the time the sexual activity took place`
        THEN JUST (`identified from the identity card` `the sex stated in the identity card`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): without a reassignment or an identity card stating a sex at the time, the subsection says nothing about how the sex is identified



§§ `s 377BB - voyeurism`

-- src:9062 | Voyeurism
-- src:9064 | 377BB.—(1) Any person (A) shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9066 | (a) intentionally observes another person (B) doing a private act without B’s
-- src:9069 | consent; and
-- src:9071 | (b) knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to being observed.
-- src:9075 | (2) Any person (A) shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9077 | (a) operates equipment with the intention of enabling A or another person to
-- src:9078 | observe a third person (B) doing a private act without B’s consent; and
-- src:9080 | (b) knows or has reason to believe that B (whether B’s private act was
-- src:9081 | recorded or not) does not consent to A operating equipment with that
-- src:9082 | intention.
-- src:9086 | (3) Any person (A) shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9088 | (a) intentionally or knowingly records another person (B) doing a private act
-- src:9089 | without B’s consent; and
-- src:9091 | (b) knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to A recording the
-- src:9092 | act.
-- src:9096 | (4) Any person (A) shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9098 | (a) operates equipment without another person’s (B) consent with the intention
-- src:9099 | of enabling A or another person (C) to observe B’s genital region, breasts if
-- src:9100 | B is female, or buttocks (whether exposed or covered) in circumstances
-- src:9101 | where the genital region, breasts, buttocks or underwear would not
-- src:9102 | otherwise be visible; and
-- src:9106 | (b) knows or has reason to believe that B (whether B’s image was recorded or
-- src:9107 | not) does not consent to A operating the equipment with that intention.
-- src:9111 | (5) Any person (A) shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9113 | (a) intentionally or knowingly records without another person’s (B) consent an
-- src:9114 | image of B’s genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks (whether
-- src:9115 | exposed or covered), in circumstances where the genital region, breasts,
-- src:9116 | buttocks or underwear would not otherwise be visible; and
-- src:9120 | (b) knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to A recording the
-- src:9121 | image.
-- src:9125 | (6) Any person (A) who installs equipment, or constructs or adapts a structure or part
-- src:9128 | of a structure, with the intention of enabling A or another person to commit an offence
-- src:9129 | under subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5) shall be guilty of an offence.
-- src:9133 | (7) Subject to subsection (8), a person who is guilty of an offence under this section
-- src:9134 | shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
-- src:9135 | 2 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any combination of such punishments.
-- src:9139 | (8) A person who commits an offence under this section against a person who is
-- src:9140 | below 14 years of age shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term
-- src:9141 | which may extend to 2 years and shall also be liable to fine or to caning.
-- src:9145 | (9) In any proceedings for an offence under this section, where a person (A) has made
-- src:9146 | a recording of another person (B) doing a private act or of B’s genital region, breasts if B
-- src:9147 | is female, or buttocks (whether exposed or covered), in circumstances where the genital
-- src:9148 | region, breasts or buttocks would not otherwise be visible, it is presumed until the
-- src:9149 | contrary is proved that B did not consent to A making the recording.
-- Six ways to commit the offence, subsections (1) to (6), one punishment, (7) and (8). "Private act" is `s 377C(3)(f) the person is doing a private act`;
-- the presumption of subsection (9) is `s 377BB(9) the effect of the recording` below.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BB (src:9062-9149)
DECLARE `Voyeurism Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person observed or recorded (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by recording B showering through a hole in the wall with a mobile phone"
    `A intentionally observes B doing a private act without B's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally observe B doing a private act (see `s 377C(3)(f) the person is doing a private act`; observation is read with `s 377C(3)(e)`), without B's consent? (s 377BB(1)(a))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to being observed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that B did not consent to being observed? (s 377BB(1)(b))
    `A operates equipment with the intention of enabling A or another person to observe a third person (B) doing a private act without B's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A operate equipment with the intention of enabling A or another person to observe a third person (B) doing a private act without B's consent? (s 377BB(2)(a))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that B (whether B's private act was recorded or not) does not consent to A operating equipment with that intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that B (whether B's private act was recorded or not) did not consent to A operating equipment with that intention? (s 377BB(2)(b))
    `A intentionally or knowingly records B doing a private act without B's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally or knowingly record B doing a private act without B's consent? (s 377BB(3)(a))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to A recording the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that B did not consent to A recording the act? (s 377BB(3)(b))
    `A operates equipment without B's consent with the intention of enabling A or another person (C) to observe B's genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks (whether exposed or covered) in circumstances where the genital region, breasts, buttocks or underwear would not otherwise be visible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A operate equipment without B's consent with the intention of enabling A or another person (C) to observe B's genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks (whether exposed or covered) in circumstances where they or the underwear would not otherwise be visible? (s 377BB(4)(a))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that B (whether B's image was recorded or not) does not consent to A operating the equipment with that intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that B (whether B's image was recorded or not) did not consent to A operating the equipment with that intention? (s 377BB(4)(b))
    `A intentionally or knowingly records without B's consent an image of B's genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks (whether exposed or covered), in circumstances where the genital region, breasts, buttocks or underwear would not otherwise be visible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally or knowingly record, without B's consent, an image of B's genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks (whether exposed or covered), in circumstances where they or the underwear would not otherwise be visible? (s 377BB(5)(a))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to A recording the image` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that B did not consent to A recording the image? (s 377BB(5)(b))
    `A installs equipment, or constructs or adapts a structure or part of a structure, with the intention of enabling A or another person to commit an offence under section 377BB(1), (2), (3), (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A install equipment, or construct or adapt a structure or part of a structure (see `s 377C(1) the thing is a structure`), with the intention of enabling A or another person to commit an offence under s 377BB(1), (2), (3), (4) or (5)? (s 377BB(6))
    `B is below 14 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person against whom the offence is committed below 14 years of age? NOT an element: it chooses which punishment s 377BB states (s 377BB(7), (8))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BB (src:9064-9129)
@export Whether the accused commits an offence under section 377BB of the Penal Code 1871 (voyeurism: observing, operating equipment to observe, recording, installing equipment)
GIVEN f IS A `Voyeurism Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits voyeurism within section 377BB` f IF
        "(1) intentionally observes another person (B) doing a private act without B's consent and knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent; (2) operates equipment with the intention of enabling A or another person to observe a third person (B) doing a private act without B's consent ...; (3) intentionally or knowingly records another person (B) doing a private act without B's consent ...; (4) operates equipment without another person's (B) consent with the intention of enabling A or another person (C) to observe B's genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks ...; (5) intentionally or knowingly records without another person's (B) consent an image of B's genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks ...; (6) installs equipment, or constructs or adapts a structure or part of a structure, with the intention of enabling A or another person to commit an offence under subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5)"
   ...    ((f's `A intentionally observes B doing a private act without B's consent` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to being observed`) OR (f's `A operates equipment with the intention of enabling A or another person to observe a third person (B) doing a private act without B's consent` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that B (whether B's private act was recorded or not) does not consent to A operating equipment with that intention`) OR (f's `A intentionally or knowingly records B doing a private act without B's consent` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to A recording the act`) OR (f's `A operates equipment without B's consent with the intention of enabling A or another person (C) to observe B's genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks (whether exposed or covered) in circumstances where the genital region, breasts, buttocks or underwear would not otherwise be visible` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that B (whether B's image was recorded or not) does not consent to A operating the equipment with that intention`) OR (f's `A intentionally or knowingly records without B's consent an image of B's genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks (whether exposed or covered), in circumstances where the genital region, breasts, buttocks or underwear would not otherwise be visible` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to A recording the image`) OR f's `A installs equipment, or constructs or adapts a structure or part of a structure, with the intention of enabling A or another person to commit an offence under section 377BB(1), (2), (3), (4) or (5)`)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BB(7) (src:9133-9135)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BB(7)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BB(7)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any combination of such punishments"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `or with`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BB(8) (src:9139-9141)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BB(8)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BB(8)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BB(7) (src:9133-9141)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 377BB(7) of the Penal Code 1871 (voyeurism)
GIVEN f IS A `Voyeurism Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 377BB(7)` f IF
        "a person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall on conviction be punished"
   ...  `commits voyeurism within section 377BB` f

GIVEN f IS A `Voyeurism Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of voyeurism not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` ((f's `A intentionally observes B doing a private act without B's consent` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to being observed`) OR (f's `A operates equipment with the intention of enabling A or another person to observe a third person (B) doing a private act without B's consent` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that B (whether B's private act was recorded or not) does not consent to A operating equipment with that intention`) OR (f's `A intentionally or knowingly records B doing a private act without B's consent` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to A recording the act`) OR (f's `A operates equipment without B's consent with the intention of enabling A or another person (C) to observe B's genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks (whether exposed or covered) in circumstances where the genital region, breasts, buttocks or underwear would not otherwise be visible` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that B (whether B's image was recorded or not) does not consent to A operating the equipment with that intention`) OR (f's `A intentionally or knowingly records without B's consent an image of B's genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks (whether exposed or covered), in circumstances where the genital region, breasts, buttocks or underwear would not otherwise be visible` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to A recording the image`) OR f's `A installs equipment, or constructs or adapts a structure or part of a structure, with the intention of enabling A or another person to commit an offence under section 377BB(1), (2), (3), (4) or (5)`) "one of the six ways in section 377BB(1) to (6): observing, operating equipment to observe, recording, operating equipment to observe the genital region, breasts or buttocks, recording an image of them, or installing equipment or a structure - each with the knowledge or reason to believe that B does not consent, except installing"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 377BB(7)` f) "the elements of section 377BB(7) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BB(7) (src:9133-9141)
@export Frame a charge under section 377BB(7) of the Penal Code 1871 (voyeurism), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Voyeurism Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 377BB(7)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "377BB(7)" "voyeurism"
        (IF f's `B is below 14 years of age` THEN `punishment prescribed by s 377BB(8)`'s words ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 377BB(7)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 377BB(7)` f)
        (CONCAT (IF f's `A intentionally observes B doing a private act without B's consent` THEN "did intentionally observe " ELSE (IF f's `A operates equipment with the intention of enabling A or another person to observe a third person (B) doing a private act without B's consent` THEN "did operate equipment with the intention of enabling the observation of " ELSE (IF f's `A intentionally or knowingly records B doing a private act without B's consent` THEN "did record " ELSE (IF f's `A operates equipment without B's consent with the intention of enabling A or another person (C) to observe B's genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks (whether exposed or covered) in circumstances where the genital region, breasts, buttocks or underwear would not otherwise be visible` THEN "did operate equipment with the intention of enabling the observation of the genital region, breasts or buttocks of " ELSE (IF f's `A intentionally or knowingly records without B's consent an image of B's genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks (whether exposed or covered), in circumstances where the genital region, breasts, buttocks or underwear would not otherwise be visible` THEN "did record an image of the genital region, breasts or buttocks of " ELSE "did install equipment, or construct or adapt a structure, with the intention of enabling the commission of an offence against "))))), (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), " without the consent of the said person, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of voyeurism not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BB(9) (src:9145-9149)
DECLARE `Presumption of non-consent to a recording` IS ONE OF
    `presumed, until the contrary is proved, not to have consented to A making the recording`
    `not covered by section 377BB(9)`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BB(9) (src:9145-9149)
@export What section 377BB(9) of the Penal Code 1871 presumes: where A has made a recording of B doing a private act, or of B's genital region, breasts or buttocks in circumstances where they would not otherwise be visible, B is presumed until the contrary is proved not to have consented to A making it
GIVEN `A has made a recording of B doing a private act, or of B's genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks (whether exposed or covered), in circumstances where the genital region, breasts or buttocks would not otherwise be visible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A make such a recording?
GIVETH A `Presumption of non-consent to a recording`
`s 377BB(9) the effect of the recording` MEANS
    IF `A has made a recording of B doing a private act, or of B's genital region, breasts if B is female, or buttocks (whether exposed or covered), in circumstances where the genital region, breasts or buttocks would not otherwise be visible`
    THEN `presumed, until the contrary is proved, not to have consented to A making the recording`
    ELSE `not covered by section 377BB(9)`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection presumes non-consent only where A has made such a recording; it does not say that B consented otherwise



§§ `s 377BC - distribution of voyeuristic image or recording`

-- src:9154 | Distribution of voyeuristic image or recording
-- src:9156 | 377BC.—(1) Any person (A) shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9158 | (a) intentionally or knowingly distributes an image or recording of another
-- src:9159 | person (B) without B’s consent to the distribution;
-- src:9161 | (b) knowing or having reason to believe that the image or recording was
-- src:9162 | obtained through the commission of an offence under section 377BB; and
-- src:9164 | (c) knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to the distribution.
-- src:9168 | (2) Any person (A) shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9170 | (a) intentionally or knowingly has in his possession an image or recording of
-- src:9171 | another person (B) for the purpose of distribution without B’s consent to
-- src:9172 | the distribution;
-- src:9174 | (b) knowing or having reason to believe that the image or recording was
-- src:9175 | obtained through the commission of an offence under section 377BB; and
-- src:9177 | (c) knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to the distribution.
-- src:9181 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), a person who is guilty of an offence under
-- src:9182 | subsection (1) or (2) shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term
-- src:9185 | which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with caning, or any combination of such
-- src:9186 | punishments.
-- src:9190 | (4) Where the image or recording in subsection (1) or (2) is of a person below
-- src:9191 | 14 years of age, a person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) or (2) shall on
-- src:9192 | conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, and
-- src:9193 | shall also be liable to fine or to caning.
-- "Distribute" is `s 377C(1) the conduct is distributing`; "image" is `s 377C(1) the thing is an image`.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BC (src:9154-9193)
DECLARE `Distribution of Voyeuristic Image Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person in the image or recording (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by posting a video of B showering to a messaging group"
    `A intentionally or knowingly distributes an image or recording of B without B's consent to the distribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally or knowingly distribute an image or recording of B without B's consent to the distribution? (s 377BC(1)(a))
    `A intentionally or knowingly has in A's possession an image or recording of B for the purpose of distribution without B's consent to the distribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally or knowingly have in A's possession an image or recording of B for the purpose of distribution without B's consent to the distribution? (s 377BC(2)(a))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained through the commission of an offence under section 377BB` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained through the commission of an offence under s 377BB? (s 377BC(1)(b), (2)(b))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to the distribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that B does not consent to the distribution? (s 377BC(1)(c), (2)(c))
    `the image or recording is of a person below 14 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image or recording of a person below 14 years of age? NOT an element: it chooses which punishment s 377BC states (s 377BC(3), (4))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BC (src:9156-9177)
@export Whether the accused commits an offence under section 377BC(1) or (2) of the Penal Code 1871 (distributing, or possessing for distribution, a voyeuristic image or recording)
GIVEN f IS A `Distribution of Voyeuristic Image Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `distributes a voyeuristic image or recording within section 377BC` f IF
        "(1)(a) intentionally or knowingly distributes an image or recording of another person (B) without B's consent to the distribution; or (2)(a) intentionally or knowingly has in his possession an image or recording of another person (B) for the purpose of distribution without B's consent to the distribution"
   ...    (f's `A intentionally or knowingly distributes an image or recording of B without B's consent to the distribution` OR f's `A intentionally or knowingly has in A's possession an image or recording of B for the purpose of distribution without B's consent to the distribution`)
   ...  "(b) knowing or having reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained through the commission of an offence under section 377BB"
   ...  f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained through the commission of an offence under section 377BB`
   ...  "(c) knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to the distribution"
   ...  f's `A knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to the distribution`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BC(3) (src:9181-9186)
