@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BC(3) (src:9181-9193)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 377BC(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (distribution of voyeuristic image or recording)
GIVEN f IS A `Distribution of Voyeuristic Image Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 377BC(3)` f IF
        "a person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) or (2) shall on conviction be punished"
   ...  `distributes a voyeuristic image or recording within section 377BC` f

GIVEN f IS A `Distribution of Voyeuristic Image Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of distribution of voyeuristic image or recording not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A intentionally or knowingly distributes an image or recording of B without B's consent to the distribution` OR f's `A intentionally or knowingly has in A's possession an image or recording of B for the purpose of distribution without B's consent to the distribution`) "A intentionally or knowingly distributes, or has in his possession for distribution, an image or recording of B without B's consent to the distribution"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained through the commission of an offence under section 377BB`) "A knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained through an offence under section 377BB"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to the distribution`) "A knows or has reason to believe that B does not consent to the distribution"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 377BC(3)` f) "the elements of section 377BC(3) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BC(3) (src:9181-9193)
@export Frame a charge under section 377BC(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (distribution of voyeuristic image or recording), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Distribution of Voyeuristic Image Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 377BC(3)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "377BC(3)" "distribution of voyeuristic image or recording"
        (IF f's `the image or recording is of a person below 14 years of age` THEN `punishment prescribed by s 377BC(4)`'s words ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 377BC(3)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 377BC(3)` f)
        (CONCAT (IF f's `A intentionally or knowingly distributes an image or recording of B without B's consent to the distribution` THEN "did distribute " ELSE "did have in your possession for distribution "), "an image or recording of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), " without the consent of the said person to the distribution, knowing or having reason to believe that it was obtained through the commission of an offence under section 377BB of the Penal Code 1871, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of distribution of voyeuristic image or recording not made out` f)


§§ `s 377BD - possession of or gaining access to voyeuristic or intimate image or recording and production of intimate image or recording`

-- src:9197 | Possession of or gaining access to voyeuristic or intimate image or recording and
-- src:9198 | production of intimate image or recording
-- src:9200 | 377BD.—(1) Any person shall be guilty of an offence who has in his possession or
-- src:9201 | has gained access to an image or recording of another person and —
-- src:9203 | (a) knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained
-- src:9204 | through the commission of an offence under section 377BB; or
-- src:9206 | (b) knows or has reason to believe that —
-- src:9207 | (i) the image or recording is an intimate image or recording as
-- src:9208 | defined in section 377BE(5);
-- src:9210 | (ii) the possession of or access to the image or recording was
-- src:9211 | without the consent of the person depicted in the image or
-- src:9212 | recording; and
-- src:9214 | (iii) the possession of or access to the image or recording will or is
-- src:9215 | likely to cause humiliation, alarm or distress to the person
-- src:9216 | depicted in the image or recording.
-- src:9220 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), a person who is guilty of an offence under subsection
-- src:9221 | (1) shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
-- src:9222 | 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- src:9227 | (3) Where the image or recording mentioned in subsection (1)(a) or (b) is of a person
-- src:9228 | below 14 years of age, a person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall on
-- src:9229 | conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, and
-- src:9230 | shall also be liable to fine or to caning.
-- src:9235 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (1) —
-- src:9238 | (a) a person has in his possession an image or recording of another person that
-- src:9239 | is in electronic form if he controls access to the electronic image or
-- src:9240 | recording, whether or not he has physical possession of the electronic
-- src:9241 | image or recording; and
-- src:9243 | (b) the ways in which a person gains access to an image or recording may
-- src:9244 | include —
-- src:9245 | (i) viewing or displaying it by an electronic medium or any other
-- src:9246 | output of the image by an electronic medium; or
-- src:9248 | (ii) communicating, sending, supplying or transmitting the image to
-- src:9249 | himself or herself.
-- src:9251 | (5) Any person who intentionally produces an intimate image or recording (as
-- src:9252 | defined in section 377BE(5)) of another person (B) —
-- src:9254 | (a) without the consent of B; and
-- src:9256 | (b) knowing or having reason to believe that the production of the image or
-- src:9257 | recording will or is likely to cause humiliation, alarm or distress to B,
-- src:9259 | shall be guilty of an offence.
-- src:9263 | (6) Subject to subsection (7), a person who is guilty of an offence under subsection
-- src:9264 | (5) shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2
-- src:9265 | years, or with fine, or with both.
-- src:9269 | (7) If the intimate image or recording mentioned in subsection (5) is of a person
-- src:9270 | below 14 years of age, a person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (5) shall on
-- src:9271 | conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, and
-- src:9272 | shall also be liable to fine or to caning.
-- src:9276 | (8) For the purposes of subsection (5), the ways in which material is produced may
-- src:9277 | include —
-- src:9279 | (a) filming, printing, photographing, recording, writing, drawing or otherwise
-- src:9280 | generating material;
-- src:9282 | (b) altering or manipulating material; or
-- src:9284 | (c) reproducing or copying material.
-- Two offences, (1) possession or access and (5) production; each has its own punishment, (2)-(3) and (6)-(7).
-- "Intimate image or recording" is `s 377BE(5) the image or recording is an intimate image or recording`, in the 377BE block below.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BD (src:9197-9284)
DECLARE `Possession of Voyeuristic Image Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person depicted (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by storing in a cloud account a video of B showering"
    `A has in A's possession or has gained access to an image or recording of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A have in A's possession (see `s 377BD(4)(a) the person has the electronic image in his possession`) or gain access to (see `s 377BD(4)(b)`) an image or recording of another person? (s 377BD(1))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained through the commission of an offence under section 377BB` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained through the commission of an offence under s 377BB? (s 377BD(1)(a))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording is an intimate image or recording as defined in section 377BE(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that the image or recording is an intimate image or recording as defined in s 377BE(5)? (s 377BD(1)(b)(i))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that the possession of or access to the image or recording was without the consent of the person depicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that the possession of or access to it was without the consent of the person depicted? (s 377BD(1)(b)(ii))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that the possession of or access to the image or recording will or is likely to cause humiliation, alarm or distress to the person depicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that the possession of or access to it will or is likely to cause humiliation, alarm or distress to the person depicted? (s 377BD(1)(b)(iii))
    `A intentionally produces an intimate image or recording (as defined in section 377BE(5)) of another person (B)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally produce an intimate image or recording (s 377BE(5)) of another person (B)? Ways of producing are read with `s 377BD(8) the way is a way of producing material` (s 377BD(5))
    `A produces it without the consent of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A produce it without the consent of B? (s 377BD(5)(a))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that the production of the image or recording will or is likely to cause humiliation, alarm or distress to B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that the production will or is likely to cause humiliation, alarm or distress to B? (s 377BD(5)(b))
    `the image or recording is of a person below 14 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image or recording of a person below 14 years of age? NOT an element: it chooses which punishment s 377BD states (s 377BD(3), (7))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BD (src:9200-9216)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 377BD(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (possession of or access to an image or recording obtained through voyeurism, or an intimate image or recording)
GIVEN f IS A `Possession of Voyeuristic Image Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `possesses or gains access to a voyeuristic or intimate image or recording within section 377BD(1)` f IF
        "Any person shall be guilty of an offence who has in his possession or has gained access to an image or recording of another person"
   ...  f's `A has in A's possession or has gained access to an image or recording of another person`
   ...  "and (a) knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained through the commission of an offence under section 377BB; or (b) knows or has reason to believe that (i) the image or recording is an intimate image or recording as defined in section 377BE(5); (ii) the possession of or access to the image or recording was without the consent of the person depicted; and (iii) the possession of or access to the image or recording will or is likely to cause humiliation, alarm or distress to the person depicted"
   ...    (f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained through the commission of an offence under section 377BB` OR (f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording is an intimate image or recording as defined in section 377BE(5)` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the possession of or access to the image or recording was without the consent of the person depicted` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the possession of or access to the image or recording will or is likely to cause humiliation, alarm or distress to the person depicted`))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BD (src:9251-9259)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 377BD(5) of the Penal Code 1871 (intentionally producing an intimate image or recording of another person without consent)
GIVEN f IS A `Possession of Voyeuristic Image Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `produces an intimate image or recording within section 377BD(5)` f IF
        "Any person who intentionally produces an intimate image or recording (as defined in section 377BE(5)) of another person (B) (a) without the consent of B; and (b) knowing or having reason to believe that the production of the image or recording will or is likely to cause humiliation, alarm or distress to B, shall be guilty of an offence"
   ...  (f's `A intentionally produces an intimate image or recording (as defined in section 377BE(5)) of another person (B)` AND f's `A produces it without the consent of B` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the production of the image or recording will or is likely to cause humiliation, alarm or distress to B`)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BD(2) (src:9220-9222)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BD(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BD(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BD(3) (src:9227-9230)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BD(3)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BD(3)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BD(2) (src:9220-9230)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 377BD(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (possession of or access to a voyeuristic or intimate image or recording)
GIVEN f IS A `Possession of Voyeuristic Image Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 377BD(2)` f IF
        "a person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall on conviction be punished"
   ...  `possesses or gains access to a voyeuristic or intimate image or recording within section 377BD(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Possession of Voyeuristic Image Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of possession of or gaining access to voyeuristic or intimate image or recording not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A has in A's possession or has gained access to an image or recording of another person`) "A has in A's possession or has gained access to an image or recording of another person"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained through the commission of an offence under section 377BB` OR (f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording is an intimate image or recording as defined in section 377BE(5)` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the possession of or access to the image or recording was without the consent of the person depicted` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the possession of or access to the image or recording will or is likely to cause humiliation, alarm or distress to the person depicted`)) "A knows or has reason to believe that the image or recording was obtained through an offence under section 377BB; or that it is an intimate image or recording, that the possession or access is without the consent of the person depicted, and that it will or is likely to cause them humiliation, alarm or distress"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 377BD(2)` f) "the elements of section 377BD(2) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BD(2) (src:9220-9230)
@export Frame a charge under section 377BD(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (possession of or access to a voyeuristic or intimate image or recording), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Possession of Voyeuristic Image Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 377BD(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "377BD(2)" "possession of or gaining access to voyeuristic or intimate image or recording"
        (IF f's `the image or recording is of a person below 14 years of age` THEN `punishment prescribed by s 377BD(3)`'s words ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 377BD(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 377BD(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "did have in your possession, or gain access to, an image or recording of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", knowing or having reason to believe that it was obtained through an offence under section 377BB of the Penal Code 1871 or that it is an intimate image or recording, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of possession of or gaining access to voyeuristic or intimate image or recording not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BD(6) (src:9263-9265)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BD(6)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BD(6)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BD(7) (src:9269-9272)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BD(7)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BD(7)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BD(6) (src:9263-9272)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 377BD(6) of the Penal Code 1871 (production of an intimate image or recording)
GIVEN f IS A `Possession of Voyeuristic Image Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 377BD(6)` f IF
        "a person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (5) shall on conviction be punished"
   ...  `produces an intimate image or recording within section 377BD(5)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Possession of Voyeuristic Image Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of production of intimate image or recording not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A intentionally produces an intimate image or recording (as defined in section 377BE(5)) of another person (B)` AND f's `A produces it without the consent of B` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the production of the image or recording will or is likely to cause humiliation, alarm or distress to B`) "A intentionally produces an intimate image or recording of B without B's consent, knowing or having reason to believe it will or is likely to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 377BD(6)` f) "the elements of section 377BD(6) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BD(6) (src:9263-9272)
@export Frame a charge under section 377BD(6) of the Penal Code 1871 (production of an intimate image or recording), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Possession of Voyeuristic Image Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 377BD(6)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "377BD(6)" "production of intimate image or recording"
        (IF f's `the image or recording is of a person below 14 years of age` THEN `punishment prescribed by s 377BD(7)`'s words ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 377BD(6)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 377BD(6)` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally produce an intimate image or recording of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), " without the consent of the said person, knowing or having reason to believe that the production would or was likely to cause the said person humiliation, alarm or distress, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of production of intimate image or recording not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BD(4)(a) (src:9238-9241)
@export Whether a person has in his possession an image or recording in electronic form, section 377BD(4)(a) of the Penal Code 1871: if he controls access to it, whether or not he has physical possession
GIVEN `the image or recording is in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image or recording in electronic form?
      `the person controls access to the electronic image or recording` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person control access to the electronic image or recording, whether or not he has physical possession of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BD(4)(a) the person has the electronic image in his possession` MEANS
    IF `the image or recording is in electronic form` AND `the person controls access to the electronic image or recording`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has in his possession an image or recording of another person that is in electronic form if he controls access to the electronic image or recording" (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BD(4)(b) (src:9243-9249)
@export Whether a way is a way in which a person gains access to an image or recording, section 377BD(4)(b) of the Penal Code 1871: the ways may include viewing or displaying it by an electronic medium, or communicating, sending, supplying or transmitting it to himself or herself
GIVEN `the person views or displays it by an electronic medium, or by any other output of the image by an electronic medium` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person view or display it by an electronic medium or any other output of the image by an electronic medium?
      `the person communicates, sends, supplies or transmits the image to himself or herself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person communicate, send, supply or transmit the image to himself or herself?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BD(4)(b) the way is a way of gaining access` MEANS
    IF `the person views or displays it by an electronic medium, or by any other output of the image by an electronic medium` OR `the person communicates, sends, supplies or transmits the image to himself or herself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "may include": the ways are not limited to these

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BD(8) (src:9276-9284)
@export Whether a way is a way in which material is produced, section 377BD(8) of the Penal Code 1871: it may include filming, printing, photographing, recording, writing, drawing or otherwise generating material, altering or manipulating material, or reproducing or copying material
GIVEN `the person films, prints, photographs, records, writes, draws or otherwise generates material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person film, print, photograph, record, write, draw or otherwise generate material?
      `the person alters or manipulates material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person alter or manipulate material?
      `the person reproduces or copies material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person reproduce or copy material?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BD(8) the way is a way of producing material` MEANS
    IF `the person films, prints, photographs, records, writes, draws or otherwise generates material` OR `the person alters or manipulates material` OR `the person reproduces or copies material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "may include": the ways are not limited to these



§§ `s 377BE - distributing or threatening to distribute intimate image or recording`

-- src:9290 | Distributing or threatening to distribute intimate image or recording
-- src:9292 | 377BE.—(1) Any person (A) shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9294 | (a) intentionally or knowingly distributes an intimate image or recording of
-- src:9295 | another person (B);
-- src:9297 | (b) without B’s consent to the distribution; and
-- src:9299 | (c) knows or has reason to believe that the distribution will or is likely to
-- src:9300 | cause B humiliation, alarm or distress.
-- src:9304 | (2) Any person (A) shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9306 | (a) knowingly threatens the distribution of an intimate image or recording of
-- src:9307 | another person (B);
-- src:9309 | (b) without B’s consent to the distribution; and
-- src:9311 | (c) knows or has reason to believe that the threat will or is likely to cause B
-- src:9312 | humiliation, alarm or distress.
-- src:9316 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), a person who is guilty of an offence under
-- src:9317 | subsection (1) or (2) shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term
-- src:9318 | which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any combination of
-- src:9319 | such punishments.
-- src:9323 | (4) A person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) against a person (B)
-- src:9324 | who is below 14 years of age shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a
-- src:9325 | term which may extend to 5 years and shall also be liable to fine or to caning.
-- src:9329 | (5) In this section, “intimate image or recording”, in relation to a person (B) —
-- src:9331 | (a) means an image or recording —
-- src:9332 | (i) of B’s genital or anal region, whether bare or covered by
-- src:9333 | underwear;
-- src:9335 | (ii) of B’s breasts if B is female, whether bare or covered by
-- src:9336 | underwear; or
-- src:9338 | (iii) of B doing a private act; and
-- src:9340 | (b) includes an image or recording, in any form, that has been altered or
-- src:9341 | generated to appear to show any of the things mentioned in paragraph (a)
-- src:9344 | but excludes an image so altered or generated that no reasonable person
-- src:9345 | would believe that it depicts B.
-- src:9347 | Illustrations
-- src:9349 | (a) A copies, crops, and pastes an image of B’s face onto the image of a body of a
-- src:9350 | person who is engaging in a sexual act. This image has been altered to appear to show
-- src:9351 | that B actually engaged in a sexual act. This is an intimate image.
-- src:9353 | (b) A pastes an image of B’s face on a cartoon depicting B performing a sexual act
-- src:9354 | on C. No reasonable person would believe that B was performing the sexual act
-- src:9355 | depicted on C. This is not an intimate image.
-- src:9359 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (2), it is not necessary for the prosecution to prove
-- src:9362 | (a) that the image or recording mentioned in the threat exists; or
-- src:9364 | (b) if the image or recording mentioned in the threat exists, that it is in fact an
-- src:9365 | intimate image or recording.
-- Subsection (5) defines "intimate image or recording": `s 377BE(5) the image or recording is an intimate image or recording`, below, with its two Illustrations.
-- Subsection (6), that the prosecution need not prove the threatened image exists or is intimate, is two functions below.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BE (src:9290-9365)
DECLARE `Intimate Image Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person depicted (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by posting a nude photograph of B to a social media account"
    `A intentionally or knowingly distributes an intimate image or recording of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally or knowingly distribute an intimate image or recording of B? (s 377BE(1)(a); see `s 377C(1) the conduct is distributing`)
    `A knowingly threatens the distribution of an intimate image or recording of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A knowingly threaten the distribution of an intimate image or recording of B? (s 377BE(2)(a))
    `the distribution (or threatened distribution) is without B's consent to the distribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it without B's consent to the distribution? (s 377BE(1)(b), (2)(b))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that the distribution will or is likely to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that the distribution will or is likely to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress? (s 377BE(1)(c))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that the threat will or is likely to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that the threat will or is likely to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress? (s 377BE(2)(c))
    `B is below 14 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B below 14 years of age? NOT an element: it chooses which punishment s 377BE states (s 377BE(3), (4))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BE (src:9292-9312)
@export Whether the accused commits an offence under section 377BE(1) or (2) of the Penal Code 1871 (distributing, or threatening to distribute, an intimate image or recording)
GIVEN f IS A `Intimate Image Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `distributes or threatens to distribute an intimate image or recording within section 377BE` f IF
        "(1) intentionally or knowingly distributes an intimate image or recording of another person (B); (b) without B's consent to the distribution; and (c) knows or has reason to believe that the distribution will or is likely to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress; or (2) knowingly threatens the distribution of an intimate image or recording of another person (B); without B's consent to the distribution; and knows or has reason to believe that the threat will or is likely to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress"
   ...    ((f's `A intentionally or knowingly distributes an intimate image or recording of B` AND f's `the distribution (or threatened distribution) is without B's consent to the distribution` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the distribution will or is likely to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress`) OR (f's `A knowingly threatens the distribution of an intimate image or recording of B` AND f's `the distribution (or threatened distribution) is without B's consent to the distribution` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the threat will or is likely to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress`))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BE(3) (src:9316-9319)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BE(3)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BE(3)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any combination of such punishments"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `or with`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BE(4) (src:9323-9325)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BE(4)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BE(4)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BE(3) (src:9316-9325)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 377BE(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (distributing or threatening to distribute an intimate image or recording)
GIVEN f IS A `Intimate Image Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 377BE(3)` f IF
        "a person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) or (2) shall on conviction be punished"
   ...  `distributes or threatens to distribute an intimate image or recording within section 377BE` f

GIVEN f IS A `Intimate Image Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of distributing or threatening to distribute intimate image or recording not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` ((f's `A intentionally or knowingly distributes an intimate image or recording of B` AND f's `the distribution (or threatened distribution) is without B's consent to the distribution` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the distribution will or is likely to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress`) OR (f's `A knowingly threatens the distribution of an intimate image or recording of B` AND f's `the distribution (or threatened distribution) is without B's consent to the distribution` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the threat will or is likely to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress`)) "A intentionally or knowingly distributes, or knowingly threatens to distribute, an intimate image or recording of B without B's consent to the distribution, knowing or having reason to believe that it will or is likely to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 377BE(3)` f) "the elements of section 377BE(3) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BE(3) (src:9316-9325)
@export Frame a charge under section 377BE(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (distributing or threatening to distribute an intimate image or recording), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Intimate Image Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 377BE(3)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "377BE(3)" "distributing or threatening to distribute intimate image or recording"
        (IF f's `B is below 14 years of age` THEN `punishment prescribed by s 377BE(4)`'s words ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 377BE(3)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 377BE(3)` f)
        (CONCAT (IF f's `A intentionally or knowingly distributes an intimate image or recording of B` THEN "did distribute an intimate image or recording of " ELSE "did threaten the distribution of an intimate image or recording of "), (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), " without the consent of the said person to the distribution, knowing or having reason to believe that it would or was likely to cause the said person humiliation, alarm or distress, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of distributing or threatening to distribute intimate image or recording not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BE(6)(a) (src:9359-9362)
@export Whether, for an offence under section 377BE(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (a threat to distribute), the prosecution must prove that the image or recording mentioned in the threat exists: it need not
GIVEN `the image or recording mentioned in the threat exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the image or recording mentioned in the threat exist? The answer changes nothing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BE(6)(a) the prosecution must prove that the image or recording mentioned in the threat exists` MEANS
    JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not necessary for the prosecution to prove (a) that the image or recording mentioned in the threat exists"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BE(6)(b) (src:9359-9365)
@export Whether, for an offence under section 377BE(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (a threat to distribute), the prosecution must prove that an existing image or recording is in fact an intimate image or recording: it need not
GIVEN `the image or recording mentioned in the threat is in fact an intimate image or recording` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image or recording mentioned in the threat, if it exists, in fact an intimate image or recording? The answer changes nothing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BE(6)(b) the prosecution must prove that the image or recording is in fact an intimate image or recording` MEANS
    JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not necessary for the prosecution to prove (b) if the image or recording mentioned in the threat exists, that it is in fact an intimate image or recording"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BE(5) (src:9329-9345)
@export Whether an image or recording is an "intimate image or recording" in relation to B within section 377BE(5) of the Penal Code 1871: an image or recording of B's genital or anal region, B's breasts if female (bare or covered by underwear), or B doing a private act, including one altered or generated to appear to show any of them, but excluding one so altered or generated that no reasonable person would believe it depicts B
GIVEN `the image or recording is of B's genital or anal region, whether bare or covered by underwear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an image or recording of B's genital or anal region, bare or covered by underwear? (s 377BE(5)(a)(i))
      `the image or recording is of B's breasts, B being female, whether bare or covered by underwear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an image or recording of B's breasts, B being female, bare or covered by underwear? (s 377BE(5)(a)(ii))
      `the image or recording is of B doing a private act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an image or recording of B doing a private act? See `s 377C(3)(f) the person is doing a private act` (s 377BE(5)(a)(iii))
      `the image or recording has been altered or generated to appear to show any of the things mentioned in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the image or recording, in any form, been altered or generated to appear to show any of those things? (s 377BE(5)(b))
      `no reasonable person would believe that the altered or generated image depicts B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so altered or generated that no reasonable person would believe that it depicts B? (s 377BE(5)(b))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BE(5) the image or recording is an intimate image or recording` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the image or recording has been altered or generated to appear to show any of the things mentioned in paragraph (a)` AND `no reasonable person would believe that the altered or generated image depicts B`
        THEN JUST FALSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but excludes an image so altered or generated that no reasonable person would believe that it depicts B"
        IF `the image or recording is of B's genital or anal region, whether bare or covered by underwear`
            OR `the image or recording is of B's breasts, B being female, whether bare or covered by underwear`
            OR `the image or recording is of B doing a private act`
            OR `the image or recording has been altered or generated to appear to show any of the things mentioned in paragraph (a)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means ... and includes ...", so an image outside both limbs is not said to fall outside the definition



§§ `s 377BF - sexual exposure`

-- src:9370 | Sexual exposure
-- src:9372 | 377BF.—(1) Any person (A) shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9374 | (a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another
-- src:9375 | person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, intentionally exposes A’s
-- src:9376 | genitals;
-- src:9378 | (b) intends that B will see A’s genitals; and
-- src:9380 | (c) does so without B’s consent.
-- src:9384 | (2) Any person (A) shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9386 | (a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another
-- src:9387 | person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, intentionally distributes to B an
-- src:9388 | image of A’s or any other person’s genitals;
-- src:9390 | (b) intends that B will see A’s or the other person’s genitals; and
-- src:9392 | (c) does so without B’s consent.
-- src:9397 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), a person who is guilty of an offence under
-- src:9398 | subsection (1) or (2) shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term
-- src:9399 | which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both.
-- src:9403 | (4) A person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) against a person (B)
-- src:9404 | who is below 14 years of age shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a
-- src:9405 | term which may extend to 2 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BF (src:9370-9405)
DECLARE `Sexual Exposure Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by exposing your genitals to B on a train"
    `A intentionally exposes A's genitals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally expose A's genitals? (s 377BF(1)(a))
    `A intentionally distributes to B an image of A's or any other person's genitals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally distribute to B an image of A's or any other person's genitals? (s 377BF(2)(a))
    `A did so for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification? (s 377BF(1)(a), (2)(a))
    `A did so for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress? (s 377BF(1)(a), (2)(a))
    `A intends that B will see the genitals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intend that B will see A's genitals (or, in s 377BF(2), A's or the other person's genitals)? (s 377BF(1)(b), (2)(b))
    `A does so without B's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A do so without B's consent? (s 377BF(1)(c), (2)(c))
    `B is below 14 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B below 14 years of age? NOT an element: it chooses which punishment s 377BF states (s 377BF(3), (4))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BF (src:9372-9392)
@export Whether the accused commits an offence under section 377BF(1) or (2) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual exposure: exposing genitals, or distributing an image of genitals, to B without B's consent)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Exposure Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits sexual exposure within section 377BF` f IF
        "(a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, intentionally exposes A's genitals, or intentionally distributes to B an image of A's or any other person's genitals"
   ...  ((f's `A intentionally exposes A's genitals` OR f's `A intentionally distributes to B an image of A's or any other person's genitals`) AND (f's `A did so for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` OR f's `A did so for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress`))
   ...  "(b) intends that B will see A's genitals (or the other person's genitals); and (c) does so without B's consent"
   ...  (f's `A intends that B will see the genitals` AND f's `A does so without B's consent`)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BF(3) (src:9397-9399)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BF(3)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BF(3)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BF(4) (src:9403-9405)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BF(4)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BF(4)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BF(3) (src:9397-9405)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 377BF(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual exposure)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Exposure Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 377BF(3)` f IF
        "a person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) or (2) shall on conviction be punished"
   ...  `commits sexual exposure within section 377BF` f

GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Exposure Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of sexual exposure not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` ((f's `A intentionally exposes A's genitals` OR f's `A intentionally distributes to B an image of A's or any other person's genitals`) AND (f's `A did so for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` OR f's `A did so for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress`)) "for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally exposes A's genitals or distributes to B an image of A's or another person's genitals"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A intends that B will see the genitals` AND f's `A does so without B's consent`) "A intends that B will see the genitals and does so without B's consent"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 377BF(3)` f) "the elements of section 377BF(3) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BF(3) (src:9397-9405)
@export Frame a charge under section 377BF(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual exposure), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Exposure Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 377BF(3)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "377BF(3)" "sexual exposure"
        (IF f's `B is below 14 years of age` THEN `punishment prescribed by s 377BF(4)`'s words ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 377BF(3)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 377BF(3)` f)
        (CONCAT "for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing humiliation, alarm or distress to ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", did intentionally ", (IF f's `A intentionally exposes A's genitals` THEN "expose your genitals" ELSE "distribute to the said person an image of genitals"), ", intending that the said person would see them, without the consent of the said person, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of sexual exposure not made out` f)


§§ `s 377BG - using or involving child in production of child abuse material`

-- src:9409 | Using or involving child in production of child abuse material
-- src:9411 | 377BG.—(1) Any person shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9413 | (a) uses a person who is below 16 years of age for the production of material
-- src:9414 | which he knows or has reason to believe is child abuse material;
-- src:9416 | (b) causes or procures a person of that age to be so used; or
-- src:9418 | (c) having the care or custody of a person of that age, consents to the person
-- src:9419 | being so used or allows the person to be so used.
-- src:9423 | (2) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall on conviction be
-- src:9424 | punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be
-- src:9425 | liable to fine or to caning.
-- src:9429 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1) —
-- src:9431 | (a) a person may have the care of a person below 16 years of age without
-- src:9432 | necessarily being entitled by law to have the custody of the child;
-- src:9434 | (b) the ways in which material is produced may include —
-- src:9435 | (i) filming, printing, photographing, recording, drawing or
-- src:9436 | otherwise generating material;
-- src:9438 | (ii) altering or manipulating material; or
-- src:9440 | (iii) reproducing or copying material; and
-- src:9442 | (c) the ways in which a person may be used in the production of material
-- src:9443 | include inviting or encouraging the person to be involved, or offering the
-- src:9444 | person to be involved, in the production of the material.
-- "Child abuse material" is `s 377C(1) the material is child abuse material`; the leaf below is set from it.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BG (src:9409-9444)
DECLARE `Child Abuse Material Use Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person below 16 years of age used in the production, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by filming the said child in a sexual pose"
    `A uses a person who is below 16 years of age for the production of material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A use a person below 16 years of age for the production of material? (s 377BG(1)(a)) Ways of using are read with `s 377BG(3)(c)`; ways of producing with `s 377BG(3)(b)`
    `A causes or procures a person below 16 years of age to be so used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A cause or procure a person below 16 years of age to be so used? (s 377BG(1)(b))
    `A, having the care or custody of a person below 16 years of age, consents to the person being so used or allows the person to be so used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A, having the care (see `s 377BG(3)(a) A has the care of the person below 16 years of age`) or custody of a person below 16 years of age, consent to the person being so used or allow the person to be so used? (s 377BG(1)(c))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that the material is child abuse material, as `s 377C(1) the material is child abuse material` says? (s 377BG(1)(a))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BG (src:9411-9419)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 377BG(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (using, or causing or allowing the use of, a person below 16 years of age in the production of child abuse material)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Use Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `uses a person below 16 years of age to produce child abuse material within section 377BG(1)` f IF
        "(a) uses a person who is below 16 years of age for the production of material; (b) causes or procures a person of that age to be so used; or (c) having the care or custody of a person of that age, consents to the person being so used or allows the person to be so used"
   ...    (f's `A uses a person who is below 16 years of age for the production of material` OR f's `A causes or procures a person below 16 years of age to be so used` OR f's `A, having the care or custody of a person below 16 years of age, consents to the person being so used or allows the person to be so used`)
   ...  "which he knows or has reason to believe is child abuse material"
   ...  f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BG(2) (src:9423-9425)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BG(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BG(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BG(2) (src:9423-9425)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 377BG(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (using or involving a child in the production of child abuse material)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Use Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 377BG(2)` f IF
        "a person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
   ...  `uses a person below 16 years of age to produce child abuse material within section 377BG(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Use Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of using or involving child in production of child abuse material not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A uses a person who is below 16 years of age for the production of material` OR f's `A causes or procures a person below 16 years of age to be so used` OR f's `A, having the care or custody of a person below 16 years of age, consents to the person being so used or allows the person to be so used`) "A uses a person below 16 years of age for the production of material, or causes or procures it, or, having the care or custody, consents or allows it"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material`) "A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 377BG(2)` f) "the elements of section 377BG(2) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BG(2) (src:9423-9425)
@export Frame a charge under section 377BG(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (using or involving a child in the production of child abuse material), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Use Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 377BG(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "377BG(2)" "using or involving child in production of child abuse material"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 377BG(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 377BG(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "did use, or cause or procure the use of, or, having the care or custody of, consent to or allow the use of, ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person below 16 years of age, for the production of material which you knew or had reason to believe was child abuse material, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of using or involving child in production of child abuse material not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BG(3)(a) (src:9431-9432)
@export Whether a person has "the care" of a person below 16 years of age, section 377BG(3)(a) of the Penal Code 1871: a person may have the care without necessarily being entitled by law to have the custody of the child
GIVEN `A in fact has the care of the person below 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A in fact have the care of the person below 16 years of age?
      `A is entitled by law to have the custody of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is A entitled by law to have the custody of the child? NOT required for care
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BG(3)(a) A has the care of the person below 16 years of age` MEANS
    IF `A in fact has the care of the person below 16 years of age`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph says care does not need legal custody; it does not say what else makes a person have the care

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BG(3)(b) (src:9434-9440)
@export Whether a way is a way in which material is produced, section 377BG(3)(b) of the Penal Code 1871: it may include filming, printing, photographing, recording, drawing or otherwise generating material, altering or manipulating material, or reproducing or copying material
GIVEN `the person films, prints, photographs, records, draws or otherwise generates material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person film, print, photograph, record, draw or otherwise generate material?
      `the person alters or manipulates material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person alter or manipulate material?
      `the person reproduces or copies material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person reproduce or copy material?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BG(3)(b) the way is a way of producing material` MEANS
    IF `the person films, prints, photographs, records, draws or otherwise generates material` OR `the person alters or manipulates material` OR `the person reproduces or copies material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "may include": the ways are not limited to these

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BG(3)(c) (src:9442-9444)
@export Whether a way is a way in which a person is used in the production of material, section 377BG(3)(c) of the Penal Code 1871: the ways include inviting or encouraging the person to be involved, or offering the person to be involved
GIVEN `the person is invited or encouraged to be involved in the production of the material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person invited or encouraged to be involved in the production of the material?
      `the person is offered to be involved in the production of the material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person offered to be involved in the production of the material?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BG(3)(c) the way is a way of using a person in the production of material` MEANS
    IF `the person is invited or encouraged to be involved in the production of the material` OR `the person is offered to be involved in the production of the material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the ways in which a person may be used in the production of material include"



§§ `s 377BH - producing child abuse material`

-- src:9448 | Producing child abuse material
-- src:9451 | 377BH.—(1) Any person who intentionally produces child abuse material knowing
-- src:9452 | or having reason to believe that the material is child abuse material shall be guilty of an
-- src:9453 | offence.
-- src:9457 | (2) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall on conviction be
-- src:9458 | punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be
-- src:9459 | liable to fine or to caning.
-- src:9463 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1), the ways in which material is produced may
-- src:9464 | include —
-- src:9466 | (a) filming, printing, photographing, recording, writing, drawing or otherwise
-- src:9467 | generating material;
-- src:9469 | (b) altering or manipulating material; or
-- src:9471 | (c) reproducing or copying material.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BH (src:9448-9471)
DECLARE `Child Abuse Material Production Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc A description of the material produced, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by drawing images of children in sexual poses"
    `A intentionally produces material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally produce material? Ways of producing are read with `s 377BH(3) the way is a way of producing material`
    `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that the material is child abuse material, as `s 377C(1) the material is child abuse material` says? (s 377BH(1))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BH (src:9451-9453)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 377BH(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (intentionally producing child abuse material)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Production Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `produces child abuse material within section 377BH(1)` f IF
        "Any person who intentionally produces child abuse material knowing or having reason to believe that the material is child abuse material shall be guilty of an offence"
   ...  (f's `A intentionally produces material` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material`)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BH(2) (src:9457-9459)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BH(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BH(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BH(2) (src:9457-9459)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 377BH(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (producing child abuse material)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Production Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 377BH(2)` f IF
        "a person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
   ...  `produces child abuse material within section 377BH(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Production Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of producing child abuse material not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A intentionally produces material` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material`) "A intentionally produces material, knowing or having reason to believe that it is child abuse material"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 377BH(2)` f) "the elements of section 377BH(2) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BH(2) (src:9457-9459)
@export Frame a charge under section 377BH(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (producing child abuse material), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Production Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 377BH(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "377BH(2)" "producing child abuse material"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 377BH(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 377BH(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally produce child abuse material, namely ", (f's victim), ", knowing or having reason to believe that it was child abuse material, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of producing child abuse material not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BH(3) (src:9463-9471)
@export Whether a way is a way in which material is produced, section 377BH(3) of the Penal Code 1871: it may include filming, printing, photographing, recording, writing, drawing or otherwise generating material, altering or manipulating material, or reproducing or copying material
GIVEN `the person films, prints, photographs, records, writes, draws or otherwise generates material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person film, print, photograph, record, write, draw or otherwise generate material?
      `the person alters or manipulates material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person alter or manipulate material?
      `the person reproduces or copies material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person reproduce or copy material?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BH(3) the way is a way of producing material` MEANS
    IF `the person films, prints, photographs, records, writes, draws or otherwise generates material` OR `the person alters or manipulates material` OR `the person reproduces or copies material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "may include": the ways are not limited to these



§§ `s 377BI - distributing or selling child abuse material`

-- src:9475 | Distributing or selling child abuse material
-- src:9477 | 377BI.—(1) Any person shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9479 | (a) distributes or sells or offers for sale child abuse material or has in the
-- src:9480 | person’s possession child abuse material for the purpose of such
-- src:9481 | distribution, sale or offer for sale; and
-- src:9483 | (b) knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material.
-- src:9487 | (2) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall on conviction be
-- src:9488 | punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be
-- src:9489 | liable to fine or to caning.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BI (src:9475-9489)
DECLARE `Child Abuse Material Distribution Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc A description of the material, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by sending the said video to a group chat"
    `A distributes or sells or offers for sale child abuse material, or has in A's possession child abuse material for the purpose of such distribution, sale or offer for sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A distribute (see `s 377C(1) the conduct is distributing`) or sell or offer for sale child abuse material, or have child abuse material in A's possession for the purpose of such distribution, sale or offer for sale? (s 377BI(1)(a))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that the material is child abuse material? (s 377BI(1)(b))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BI (src:9477-9483)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 377BI(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (distributing or selling child abuse material, or possessing it for that purpose)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Distribution Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `distributes or sells child abuse material within section 377BI(1)` f IF
        "(a) distributes or sells or offers for sale child abuse material or has in the person's possession child abuse material for the purpose of such distribution, sale or offer for sale; and (b) knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material"
   ...  (f's `A distributes or sells or offers for sale child abuse material, or has in A's possession child abuse material for the purpose of such distribution, sale or offer for sale` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material`)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BI(2) (src:9487-9489)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BI(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BI(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BI(2) (src:9487-9489)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 377BI(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (distributing or selling child abuse material)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Distribution Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 377BI(2)` f IF
        "a person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
   ...  `distributes or sells child abuse material within section 377BI(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Distribution Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of distributing or selling child abuse material not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A distributes or sells or offers for sale child abuse material, or has in A's possession child abuse material for the purpose of such distribution, sale or offer for sale` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material`) "A distributes or sells or offers for sale child abuse material, or has it for that purpose, knowing or having reason to believe that it is child abuse material"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 377BI(2)` f) "the elements of section 377BI(2) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BI(2) (src:9487-9489)
@export Frame a charge under section 377BI(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (distributing or selling child abuse material), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Distribution Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 377BI(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "377BI(2)" "distributing or selling child abuse material"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 377BI(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 377BI(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "did distribute, or sell, or offer for sale, or have in your possession for such distribution, sale or offer for sale, child abuse material, namely ", (f's victim), ", knowing or having reason to believe that it was child abuse material, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of distributing or selling child abuse material not made out` f)


§§ `s 377BJ - advertising or seeking child abuse material`

-- src:9493 | Advertising or seeking child abuse material
-- src:9495 | 377BJ.—(1) Any person shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9496 | (a) for the purposes of distributing or selling or offering for sale any child
-- src:9497 | abuse material advertises the material; and
-- src:9499 | (b) knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material.
-- src:9503 | (2) Any person shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9504 | (a) announces or otherwise makes known by any means any offer or purported
-- src:9507 | offer to acquire, buy or gain access to any child abuse material; and
-- src:9509 | (b) knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material.
-- src:9513 | (3) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) or (2) shall on
-- src:9514 | conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, and
-- src:9515 | shall also be liable to fine or to caning.
-- src:9519 | (4) In subsection (1), “advertise”, in relation to child abuse material, includes —
-- src:9521 | (a) exhibiting, displaying or supplying any advertising material relating to the
-- src:9522 | material;
-- src:9524 | (b) announcing by any means any offer to sell or distribute the material; or
-- src:9526 | (c) distributing or circulating any advertisement relating to the material.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BJ (src:9493-9526)
DECLARE `Child Abuse Material Advertising Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc A description of the material, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by posting an advertisement on an online forum"
    `A, for the purposes of distributing or selling or offering for sale any child abuse material, advertises the material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A, for the purposes of distributing or selling or offering for sale any child abuse material, advertise the material? "Advertise" is read with `s 377BJ(4) the conduct is advertising` (s 377BJ(1)(a))
    `A announces or otherwise makes known by any means any offer or purported offer to acquire, buy or gain access to any child abuse material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A announce or otherwise make known by any means any offer or purported offer to acquire, buy or gain access to any child abuse material? (s 377BJ(2)(a))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that the material is child abuse material? (s 377BJ(1)(b), (2)(b))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BJ (src:9495-9509)
@export Whether the accused commits an offence under section 377BJ(1) or (2) of the Penal Code 1871 (advertising child abuse material for distribution or sale, or announcing an offer to acquire or gain access to it)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Advertising Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `advertises or seeks child abuse material within section 377BJ` f IF
        "(1)(a) for the purposes of distributing or selling or offering for sale any child abuse material advertises the material; or (2)(a) announces or otherwise makes known by any means any offer or purported offer to acquire, buy or gain access to any child abuse material"
   ...    (f's `A, for the purposes of distributing or selling or offering for sale any child abuse material, advertises the material` OR f's `A announces or otherwise makes known by any means any offer or purported offer to acquire, buy or gain access to any child abuse material`)
   ...  "and knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material"
   ...  f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BJ(3) (src:9513-9515)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BJ(3)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BJ(3)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BJ(3) (src:9513-9515)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 377BJ(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (advertising or seeking child abuse material)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Advertising Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 377BJ(3)` f IF
        "a person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) or (2) shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
   ...  `advertises or seeks child abuse material within section 377BJ` f

GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Advertising Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of advertising or seeking child abuse material not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A, for the purposes of distributing or selling or offering for sale any child abuse material, advertises the material` OR f's `A announces or otherwise makes known by any means any offer or purported offer to acquire, buy or gain access to any child abuse material`) "A advertises child abuse material for distribution or sale, or announces an offer to acquire, buy or gain access to it"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material`) "A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 377BJ(3)` f) "the elements of section 377BJ(3) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BJ(3) (src:9513-9515)
@export Frame a charge under section 377BJ(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (advertising or seeking child abuse material), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Advertising Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 377BJ(3)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "377BJ(3)" "advertising or seeking child abuse material"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 377BJ(3)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 377BJ(3)` f)
        (CONCAT (IF f's `A, for the purposes of distributing or selling or offering for sale any child abuse material, advertises the material` THEN "did advertise child abuse material for the purpose of distributing or selling or offering it for sale, namely " ELSE "did announce or make known an offer to acquire, buy or gain access to child abuse material, namely "), (f's victim), ", knowing or having reason to believe that it was child abuse material, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of advertising or seeking child abuse material not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BJ(4) (src:9519-9526)
@export Whether conduct is to "advertise" child abuse material within section 377BJ(4) of the Penal Code 1871: it includes exhibiting, displaying or supplying advertising material, announcing an offer to sell or distribute, or distributing or circulating an advertisement
GIVEN `the conduct is exhibiting, displaying or supplying any advertising material relating to the material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conduct exhibiting, displaying or supplying any advertising material relating to the material?
      `the conduct is announcing by any means any offer to sell or distribute the material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conduct announcing by any means any offer to sell or distribute the material?
      `the conduct is distributing or circulating any advertisement relating to the material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conduct distributing or circulating any advertisement relating to the material?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BJ(4) the conduct is advertising` MEANS
    IF `the conduct is exhibiting, displaying or supplying any advertising material relating to the material` OR `the conduct is announcing by any means any offer to sell or distribute the material` OR `the conduct is distributing or circulating any advertisement relating to the material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "\"advertise\", in relation to child abuse material, includes"



§§ `s 377BK - possession of or gaining access to child abuse material`

-- src:9530 | Possession of or gaining access to child abuse material
-- src:9532 | 377BK.—(1) Any person shall be guilty of an offence who —
-- src:9534 | (a) has in the person’s possession or has gained access to child abuse material;
-- src:9535 | and
-- src:9537 | (b) knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material.
-- src:9541 | (2) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall on conviction be
-- src:9542 | punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, and shall also be
-- src:9543 | liable to fine or to caning.
-- src:9547 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1) —
-- src:9549 | (a) a person has in the person’s possession child abuse material that is
-- src:9550 | electronic material if the person controls access to the material whether or
-- src:9551 | not the person has physical possession of the electronic material; and
-- src:9553 | (b) the ways in which a person gains access to material may include viewing
-- src:9554 | material or displaying material by an electronic medium or any other
-- src:9555 | output of the material by an electronic medium.
-- src:9557 | Illustration
-- src:9559 | Y has an online storage account for electronic material accessible with a username
-- src:9562 | and password. Y has control of what is stored in the account and can upload to, copy
-- src:9563 | from or delete material from the account. Y has an electronic folder in the account to
-- src:9564 | which Y uploads and stores electronic child abuse material. Y has in his possession
-- src:9565 | child abuse material.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BK (src:9530-9565)
DECLARE `Child Abuse Material Possession Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc A description of the material, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by storing the said video in a cloud account"
    `A has in A's possession or has gained access to child abuse material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A have in A's possession (see `s 377BK(3)(a) the person has the electronic child abuse material in his possession`) or gain access to (see `s 377BK(3)(b)`) child abuse material? (s 377BK(1)(a))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or have reason to believe that the material is child abuse material? (s 377BK(1)(b))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BK (src:9532-9537)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 377BK(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (possession of or access to child abuse material)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Possession Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `possesses or gains access to child abuse material within section 377BK(1)` f IF
        "(a) has in the person's possession or has gained access to child abuse material; and (b) knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material"
   ...  (f's `A has in A's possession or has gained access to child abuse material` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material`)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BK(2) (src:9541-9543)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BK(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BK(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BK(2) (src:9541-9543)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 377BK(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (possession of or gaining access to child abuse material)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Possession Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 377BK(2)` f IF
        "a person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
   ...  `possesses or gains access to child abuse material within section 377BK(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Possession Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of possession of or gaining access to child abuse material not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A has in A's possession or has gained access to child abuse material` AND f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the material is child abuse material`) "A has in A's possession or has gained access to child abuse material, knowing or having reason to believe that it is child abuse material"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 377BK(2)` f) "the elements of section 377BK(2) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BK(2) (src:9541-9543)
@export Frame a charge under section 377BK(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (possession of or gaining access to child abuse material), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Possession Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 377BK(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "377BK(2)" "possession of or gaining access to child abuse material"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 377BK(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 377BK(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "did have in your possession, or gain access to, child abuse material, namely ", (f's victim), ", knowing or having reason to believe that it was child abuse material, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of possession of or gaining access to child abuse material not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BK(3)(a) (src:9549-9551)
@export Whether a person has in his possession child abuse material that is electronic material, section 377BK(3)(a) of the Penal Code 1871: if the person controls access to it, whether or not he has physical possession
GIVEN `the child abuse material is electronic material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child abuse material electronic material?
      `the person controls access to the material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person control access to the material, whether or not he has physical possession of it? (See the Illustration: control of an online storage account)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BK(3)(a) the person has the electronic child abuse material in his possession` MEANS
    IF `the child abuse material is electronic material` AND `the person controls access to the material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has in the person's possession child abuse material that is electronic material if the person controls access to the material whether or not the person has physical possession" (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BK(3)(b) (src:9553-9555)
@export Whether a way is a way in which a person gains access to material, section 377BK(3)(b) of the Penal Code 1871: the ways may include viewing material or displaying it by an electronic medium or any other output of it by an electronic medium
GIVEN `the person views the material or displays it by an electronic medium or any other output of the material by an electronic medium` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person view the material or display it by an electronic medium or any other output of the material by an electronic medium?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BK(3)(b) the way is a way of gaining access to material` MEANS
    IF `the person views the material or displays it by an electronic medium or any other output of the material by an electronic medium`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "may include": the ways are not limited to this



§§ `s 377BL - exploitation by abusive material of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`

-- src:9569 | Exploitation by abusive material of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age
-- src:9571 | 377BL.—(1) This section applies only where a person (A) is in a relationship with
-- src:9572 | another person (B) who is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age, that is exploitative
-- src:9573 | of B.
-- src:9577 | (2) A person (A) who uses B for the production of material which A knows or has
-- src:9578 | reason to believe is abusive material or causes or procures B to be so used shall be guilty
-- src:9579 | of an offence and shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which
-- src:9580 | may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning.
-- src:9584 | (3) A person (A) who intentionally produces abusive material of B shall be guilty of
-- src:9585 | an offence and shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
-- src:9586 | extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning.
-- src:9590 | (4) A person (A) who distributes or sells or offers for sale abusive material of B or has
-- src:9591 | in A’s possession abusive material of B for the purpose of such distribution, sale or offer
-- src:9592 | for sale; and knowing or having reason to believe that the material is abusive material of
-- src:9593 | B shall be guilty of an offence and shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment
-- src:9594 | for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning.
-- src:9598 | (5) For the purposes of this section —
-- src:9600 | (a) the ways in which material is produced may include —
-- src:9601 | (i) filming, printing, photographing, recording, writing, drawing or
-- src:9602 | otherwise generating material;
-- src:9604 | (ii) altering or manipulating material; or
-- src:9606 | (iii) reproducing or copying material; and
-- src:9608 | (b) the ways in which a person may be used in the production of material
-- src:9609 | include inviting or encouraging the person to be involved, or offering the
-- src:9610 | person to be involved, in the production of the material.
-- src:9615 | (6) In this section, “abusive material”, in relation to B, means material that depicts —
-- src:9617 | (a) an image of B —
-- src:9618 | (i) as a victim of torture, cruelty or physical abuse (whether or not
-- src:9619 | the torture, cruelty or abuse is sexual);
-- src:9621 | (ii) as a victim of sexual abuse;
-- src:9623 | (iii) engaged in, or apparently engaging in, a sexual pose or sexual
-- src:9624 | activity (whether or not in the presence of another person); or
-- src:9626 | (iv) in the presence of another person who is engaged in, or
-- src:9627 | apparently engaged in a sexual pose or sexual activity;
-- src:9629 | (b) the genital region or buttocks (whether exposed or covered) of B, where
-- src:9630 | the depiction is sexual and in circumstances (whether or not apparent from
-- src:9631 | the depiction) which reasonable persons would regard as being offensive;
-- src:9632 | or
-- src:9636 | (c) the breasts (whether exposed or covered) of B if B is female, where the
-- src:9637 | depiction is sexual and in circumstances (whether or not apparent from the
-- src:9638 | depiction) which reasonable persons would regard as being offensive.
-- Subsection (1): the section applies only where the relationship is exploitative; the first two leaves are part of every offence below.
-- "Abusive material" is `s 377BL(6) the material is abusive material`; ways of producing and using are `s 377BL(5)(a)` and `(b)`.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BL (src:9569-9638)
DECLARE `Exploitative Abusive Material Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by filming B in a sexual pose"
    `A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is A in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B, as the court determines under s 377CA? (s 377BL(1))
    `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B of or above 16 but below 18 years of age? Set from the helper `of or above 16 years of age but below 18 years of age` on B's age (s 377BL(1))
    `A uses B for the production of material which A knows or has reason to believe is abusive material, or causes or procures B to be so used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A use B for the production of material which A knows or has reason to believe is abusive material, or cause or procure B to be so used? (s 377BL(2))
    `A intentionally produces abusive material of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally produce abusive material of B? (s 377BL(3))
    `A distributes or sells or offers for sale abusive material of B, or has in A's possession abusive material of B for the purpose of such distribution, sale or offer for sale, knowing or having reason to believe that the material is abusive material of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A distribute or sell or offer for sale abusive material of B, or have it in A's possession for that purpose, knowing or having reason to believe that the material is abusive material of B? (s 377BL(4))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BL (src:9571-9580)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 377BL(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (using a minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age in an exploitative relationship to produce abusive material)
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Abusive Material Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `uses an exploitatively related minor to produce abusive material within section 377BL(2)` f IF
        "(1) This section applies only where a person (A) is in a relationship with another person (B) who is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age, that is exploitative of B"
   ...  (f's `A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B` AND f's `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`)
   ...  "(2) A person (A) who uses B for the production of material which A knows or has reason to believe is abusive material or causes or procures B to be so used shall be guilty of an offence"
   ...  f's `A uses B for the production of material which A knows or has reason to believe is abusive material, or causes or procures B to be so used`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BL (src:9571-9586)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 377BL(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (intentionally producing abusive material of a minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age in an exploitative relationship)
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Abusive Material Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `produces abusive material of an exploitatively related minor within section 377BL(3)` f IF
        "(1) This section applies only where a person (A) is in a relationship with another person (B) who is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age, that is exploitative of B"
   ...  (f's `A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B` AND f's `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`)
   ...  "(3) A person (A) who intentionally produces abusive material of B shall be guilty of an offence"
   ...  f's `A intentionally produces abusive material of B`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BL (src:9571-9594)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 377BL(4) of the Penal Code 1871 (distributing or selling abusive material of a minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age in an exploitative relationship)
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Abusive Material Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `distributes abusive material of an exploitatively related minor within section 377BL(4)` f IF
        "(1) This section applies only where a person (A) is in a relationship with another person (B) who is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age, that is exploitative of B"
   ...  (f's `A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B` AND f's `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`)
   ...  "(4) A person (A) who distributes or sells or offers for sale abusive material of B or has in A's possession abusive material of B for the purpose of such distribution, sale or offer for sale; and knowing or having reason to believe that the material is abusive material of B shall be guilty of an offence"
   ...  f's `A distributes or sells or offers for sale abusive material of B, or has in A's possession abusive material of B for the purpose of such distribution, sale or offer for sale, knowing or having reason to believe that the material is abusive material of B`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BL(2) (src:9578-9580)
`punishment prescribed by s 377BL(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BL(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BL(2) (src:9577-9580)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 377BL(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (using an exploitatively related minor to produce abusive material)
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Abusive Material Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 377BL(2)` f IF
        "shall be guilty of an offence and shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
   ...  `uses an exploitatively related minor to produce abusive material within section 377BL(2)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Abusive Material Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of using exploitatively related minor to produce abusive material not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B` AND f's `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`) "A is in a relationship with B, who is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age, that is exploitative of B"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A uses B for the production of material which A knows or has reason to believe is abusive material, or causes or procures B to be so used`) "A uses B for the production of abusive material, or causes or procures B to be so used"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 377BL(2)` f) "the elements of section 377BL(2) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BL(2) (src:9577-9580)
@export Frame a charge under section 377BL(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (using an exploitatively related minor to produce abusive material), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Abusive Material Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 377BL(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "377BL(2)" "using exploitatively related minor to produce abusive material"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 377BL(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 377BL(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "being in a relationship that is exploitative of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age, did use, or cause or procure the use of, the said person for the production of material which you knew or had reason to believe was abusive material, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of using exploitatively related minor to produce abusive material not made out` f)

