    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "377BL(4)" "distributing abusive material of exploitatively related minor"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 377BL(4)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 377BL(4)` f)
        (CONCAT "being in a relationship that is exploitative of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age, did distribute or sell or offer for sale abusive material of the said person, or have it in your possession for that purpose, knowing or having reason to believe that it was abusive material, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of distributing abusive material of exploitatively related minor not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BL(5)(a) (src:9600-9606)
@export Whether a way is a way in which material is produced, section 377BL(5)(a) of the Penal Code 1871: it may include filming, printing, photographing, recording, writing, drawing or otherwise generating material, altering or manipulating material, or reproducing or copying material
GIVEN `the person films, prints, photographs, records, writes, draws or otherwise generates material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person film, print, photograph, record, write, draw or otherwise generate material?
      `the person alters or manipulates material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person alter or manipulate material?
      `the person reproduces or copies material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person reproduce or copy material?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BL(5)(a) the way is a way of producing material` MEANS
    IF `the person films, prints, photographs, records, writes, draws or otherwise generates material` OR `the person alters or manipulates material` OR `the person reproduces or copies material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "may include": the ways are not limited to these

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BL(5)(b) (src:9608-9610)
@export Whether a way is a way in which a person is used in the production of material, section 377BL(5)(b) of the Penal Code 1871: the ways include inviting or encouraging the person to be involved, or offering the person to be involved
GIVEN `the person is invited or encouraged to be involved in the production of the material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person invited or encouraged to be involved in the production of the material?
      `the person is offered to be involved in the production of the material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person offered to be involved in the production of the material?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BL(5)(b) the way is a way of using a person in the production of material` MEANS
    IF `the person is invited or encouraged to be involved in the production of the material` OR `the person is offered to be involved in the production of the material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the ways in which a person may be used in the production of material include"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BL(6) (src:9615-9638)
@export Whether material is "abusive material" in relation to B within section 377BL(6) of the Penal Code 1871: material depicting B as a victim of abuse, in a sexual pose or activity or in the presence of another in one, or the sexual and offensive depiction of B's genital region, buttocks or (if female) breasts
GIVEN `the image is of B as a victim of torture, cruelty or physical abuse (whether or not the torture, cruelty or abuse is sexual)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image of B as a victim of torture, cruelty or physical abuse, whether or not sexual? (s 377BL(6)(a)(i))
      `the image is of B as a victim of sexual abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image of B as a victim of sexual abuse? (s 377BL(6)(a)(ii))
      `the image is of B engaged in, or apparently engaging in, a sexual pose or sexual activity (whether or not in the presence of another person)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image of B engaged in, or apparently engaging in, a sexual pose or sexual activity, whether or not in the presence of another person? (s 377BL(6)(a)(iii))
      `the image is of B in the presence of another person who is engaged in, or apparently engaged in, a sexual pose or sexual activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image of B in the presence of another person who is engaged in, or apparently engaged in, a sexual pose or sexual activity? (s 377BL(6)(a)(iv))
      `the material depicts the genital region or buttocks (whether exposed or covered) of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material depict the genital region or buttocks (whether exposed or covered) of B? (s 377BL(6)(b))
      `the material depicts the breasts (whether exposed or covered) of B, who is female` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material depict the breasts (whether exposed or covered) of B, if B is female? (s 377BL(6)(c))
      `the depiction is sexual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the depiction sexual? See `s 377C(3)(d) the conduct is sexual`
      `reasonable persons would regard the circumstances as offensive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances (whether or not apparent from the depiction) such that reasonable persons would regard them as offensive?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BL(6) the material is abusive material` MEANS
    IF `the image is of B as a victim of torture, cruelty or physical abuse (whether or not the torture, cruelty or abuse is sexual)` OR `the image is of B as a victim of sexual abuse` OR `the image is of B engaged in, or apparently engaging in, a sexual pose or sexual activity (whether or not in the presence of another person)` OR `the image is of B in the presence of another person who is engaged in, or apparently engaged in, a sexual pose or sexual activity` OR ((`the material depicts the genital region or buttocks (whether exposed or covered) of B` OR `the material depicts the breasts (whether exposed or covered) of B, who is female`) AND `the depiction is sexual` AND `reasonable persons would regard the circumstances as offensive`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"abusive material\", in relation to B, means material that depicts ..."



§§ `s 377BM - defences to offences relating to intimate image or recording and voyeurism`

-- src:9643 | Defences to offences relating to intimate image or recording and voyeurism
-- src:9645 | 377BM.—(1) It is a defence to a charge for an offence under section 377BD of
-- src:9646 | having possession of or gained access to an image or a recording obtained through the
-- src:9647 | commission of an offence under section 377BB or an intimate image or recording
-- src:9648 | mentioned in section 377BD(1)(b) for the accused person to prove that the accused
-- src:9649 | person —
-- src:9651 | (a) did not intentionally come into possession of or gain access to the image or
-- src:9652 | recording; and
-- src:9654 | (b) on becoming aware of having come into possession of or gaining access to
-- src:9655 | the image or recording, as soon as it was practicable to do so, took all
-- src:9656 | reasonable steps in the circumstances to cease possession of or access to
-- src:9657 | the image or recording.
-- src:9661 | (2) It is a defence to a charge for an offence under section 377BB, 377BC, 377BD or
-- src:9662 | 377BE(1) if —
-- src:9665 | (a) the act that is alleged to constitute the offence was done for any of the
-- src:9666 | following purposes without intent to cause injury to the person (B)
-- src:9667 | mentioned in section 377BB(1), (2), (3), (4) or (5), 377BC(1) or (2) or
-- src:9668 | 377BE(1) or the person depicted in the intimate image or recording
-- src:9669 | mentioned in section 377BD(1)(b) or (5), and with reasonable cause:
-- src:9671 | (i) the prevention, detection, investigation or punishment of any
-- src:9672 | offence;
-- src:9674 | (ii) the conduct of contemplated or pending proceedings in any
-- src:9675 | court or tribunal or to obtain evidence for the purpose of
-- src:9676 | contemplating such proceedings;
-- src:9678 | (iii) safety or national security; and
-- src:9683 | (b) the image or recording (if any) obtained through the commission of an
-- src:9684 | offence under section 377BB or the intimate image or recording (if any)
-- src:9685 | mentioned in section 377BD(1)(b) or (5) or 377BE(5) was not kept for a
-- src:9686 | period longer than what was reasonably necessary or required for the
-- src:9687 | purposes mentioned in paragraph (a).
-- src:9689 | Illustrations
-- src:9691 | (a) A, a caregiver is concerned that B, an elderly person has been in the toilet for an
-- src:9692 | unusually long period of time. Despite A knocking several times, there is no response
-- src:9693 | from B. As A is concerned for B’s safety, A forcefully opens the toilet door to find B in
-- src:9694 | a state of undress. A has committed no offence as the act was done for the purpose of
-- src:9695 | ensuring B’s safety.
-- src:9697 | (b) A notices that a stranger is using a mobile phone taking an upskirt photograph
-- src:9698 | of a woman in the mall. A confronts the stranger who flees and drops his mobile
-- src:9699 | phone. A keeps the mobile phone with the upskirt photograph with the intention of
-- src:9700 | reporting the offence to the police. A hands over the phone to the police when he
-- src:9701 | makes the police report. A has committed no offence as the act of possession of the
-- src:9702 | upskirt photograph was done for the purpose of assisting the detection or investigation
-- src:9703 | of the offence.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BM (src:9643-9703)
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BM(1) (src:9645-9657)
@export Whether the defence in section 377BM(1) of the Penal Code 1871 is made out for a charge under section 377BD of possession of or access to an image or recording obtained through an offence under 377BB or an intimate image or recording: the accused proves the possession or access was not intentional and, on becoming aware, all reasonable steps to cease it were taken as soon as practicable
GIVEN `the charge is under section 377BD of having possession of or gained access to an image or recording obtained through an offence under section 377BB or an intimate image or recording mentioned in section 377BD(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge one under s 377BD of having possession of or having gained access to such an image or recording?
      `the accused person did not intentionally come into possession of or gain access to the image or recording` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the accused proved that he or she did not intentionally come into possession of or gain access to it? (s 377BM(1)(a))
      `on becoming aware, as soon as it was practicable to do so, the accused person took all reasonable steps in the circumstances to cease possession of or access to the image or recording` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the accused proved that, on becoming aware, as soon as it was practicable, he or she took all reasonable steps in the circumstances to cease possession of or access to it? (s 377BM(1)(b))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BM(1) the defence of unintended possession or access is made out` MEANS
    IF `the charge is under section 377BD of having possession of or gained access to an image or recording obtained through an offence under section 377BB or an intimate image or recording mentioned in section 377BD(1)(b)` AND `the accused person did not intentionally come into possession of or gain access to the image or recording` AND `on becoming aware, as soon as it was practicable to do so, the accused person took all reasonable steps in the circumstances to cease possession of or access to the image or recording`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says what the accused can prove to have a defence; it does not say that an accused who cannot prove it has none

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BM(2) (src:9661-9687)
@export Whether the defence in section 377BM(2) of the Penal Code 1871 is made out for a charge under section 377BB, 377BC, 377BD or 377BE(1): the act was done for the prevention, detection, investigation or punishment of an offence, proceedings, or safety or national security, without intent to cause injury and with reasonable cause, and the image or recording was not kept longer than reasonably necessary
GIVEN `the charge is under section 377BB, 377BC, 377BD or 377BE(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge one under s 377BB, 377BC, 377BD or 377BE(1)?
      `the act was done for the prevention, detection, investigation or punishment of any offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done for the prevention, detection, investigation or punishment of any offence?
      `the act was done for the conduct of contemplated or pending proceedings in any court or tribunal, or to obtain evidence for the purpose of contemplating such proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done for the conduct of contemplated or pending proceedings in any court or tribunal, or to obtain evidence for the purpose of contemplating such proceedings?
      `the act was done for safety or national security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done for safety or national security?
      `the act was done without intent to cause injury to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done without intent to cause injury to the person (B) or the person depicted?
      `the act was done with reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done with reasonable cause?
      `the image or recording was not kept for a period longer than what was reasonably necessary or required for the purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the image or recording (if any) not kept for a period longer than what was reasonably necessary or required for those purposes? (s 377BM(2)(b))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BM(2) the defence of a protected purpose is made out` MEANS
    IF `the charge is under section 377BB, 377BC, 377BD or 377BE(1)` AND (`the act was done for the prevention, detection, investigation or punishment of any offence` OR `the act was done for the conduct of contemplated or pending proceedings in any court or tribunal, or to obtain evidence for the purpose of contemplating such proceedings` OR `the act was done for safety or national security`) AND `the act was done without intent to cause injury to the person` AND `the act was done with reasonable cause` AND `the image or recording was not kept for a period longer than what was reasonably necessary or required for the purposes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence to a charge for an offence under section 377BB, 377BC, 377BD or 377BE(1) if (a) the act ... was done for any of the following purposes without intent to cause injury ... and with reasonable cause ...; (b) the image or recording ... was not kept for a period longer than ..." (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)



§§ `s 377BN - defences to child abuse material offences`

-- src:9708 | Defences to child abuse material offences
-- src:9710 | 377BN.—(1) It is a defence to a charge for an offence of having possession of or
-- src:9711 | gaining access to child abuse material under section 377BK for the accused person to
-- src:9714 | prove that the accused person —
-- src:9716 | (a) did not intentionally come into possession of or gain access to child abuse
-- src:9717 | material; and
-- src:9719 | (b) on becoming aware of having come into possession of or gaining access to
-- src:9720 | child abuse material, as soon as it was practicable to do so, took all
-- src:9721 | reasonable steps in the circumstances to cease possession of or access to
-- src:9722 | the material.
-- src:9726 | (2) It is a defence to a charge for an offence under sections 377BH to 377BK if —
-- src:9728 | (a) the act that is alleged to constitute the offence was done for any of the
-- src:9729 | following purposes without intent to cause injury to the person depicted in
-- src:9730 | the child abuse material and with reasonable cause:
-- src:9731 | (i) the prevention, detection, investigation or punishment of any
-- src:9732 | offence;
-- src:9734 | (ii) the conduct of contemplated or pending proceedings in any
-- src:9735 | court or tribunal or to obtain evidence for the purpose of
-- src:9736 | contemplating such proceedings;
-- src:9738 | (iii) safety or national security; and
-- src:9742 | (b) the child abuse material was not kept for a period longer than what was
-- src:9743 | reasonably necessary or required for the purposes mentioned in
-- src:9744 | paragraph (a).
-- src:9749 | (3) It is a defence to a charge for an offence under sections 377BH to 377BK if the
-- src:9750 | act that is alleged to constitute the offence —
-- src:9752 | (a) has a legitimate purpose related to science, medicine, education or art; and
-- src:9754 | (b) did not pose an undue risk of harm to any person below 16 years of age.
-- src:9756 | Explanation.—An act has a legitimate purpose related to art which reasonable
-- src:9757 | persons would regard as art.
-- src:9759 | Illustrations
-- src:9761 | (a) A university researcher has child abuse material in his possession for the
-- src:9762 | purposes of studying the psychological effects of exposure to such material. The
-- src:9763 | researcher’s possession of the child abuse material has a legitimate purpose.
-- src:9766 | (b) A is a photo-journalist in a war zone. A takes a photo of a child victim of torture
-- src:9767 | and submits this together with an article on the plight of such children to a news
-- src:9768 | organisation for publication. The taking and sending of the photo has a legitimate
-- src:9769 | purpose.
-- src:9773 | (4) It is a defence to a charge for an offence under sections 377BH to 377BK if —
-- src:9775 | (a) the accused person (A) is below 16 years of age; and
-- src:9777 | (b) the child abuse material that is alleged to constitute the offence is an image
-- src:9778 | of A alone.
-- src:9780 | Illustration
-- src:9782 | A is 15 years old and takes a photo of herself alone posing in the nude. A stores the
-- src:9783 | photo in her mobile phone. A has not committed the offence of producing or
-- src:9784 | possessing child abuse material.
-- src:9788 | (5) To avoid doubt, it is not a defence to a charge for an offence relating to child
-- src:9789 | abuse material or abusive material (as the case may be) under sections 377BG to 377BL
-- src:9790 | that, at the time of the conduct constituting the offence, the accused was under a
-- src:9791 | mistaken but honest and reasonable belief that reasonable persons would not regard the
-- src:9792 | child abuse material or abusive material (as the case may be) as being, in the
-- src:9793 | circumstances, offensive.
-- src:9798 | (6) It is a defence to a charge for the following offences in circumstances where the
-- src:9799 | offender (A) and the person below 16 years of age (B) are married and subject to the
-- src:9800 | following respective conditions:
-- src:9802 | (a) an offence under section 377BG(1) or 377BH(1) if the child abuse
-- src:9803 | material —
-- src:9804 | (i) involves only A and B in its production;
-- src:9806 | (ii) depicts B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of
-- src:9807 | age; and
-- src:9809 | (iii) was produced with B’s consent;
-- src:9811 | (b) an offence under section 377BI if the distribution of the child abuse
-- src:9814 | material —
-- src:9815 | (i) occurs between A and B only;
-- src:9817 | (ii) involves material depicting B only, A and B only, or A only if A
-- src:9818 | is below 16 years of age; and
-- src:9820 | (iii) was distributed with B’s consent;
-- src:9822 | (c) an offence under section 377BJ(2) if the offer to acquire, buy, or gain
-- src:9823 | access to the child abuse material —
-- src:9824 | (i) occurs between A and B only; and
-- src:9826 | (ii) involves material depicting B only, A and B only, or A only if A
-- src:9827 | is below 16 years of age;
-- src:9829 | (d) an offence under section 377BK(1) if the possession of the child abuse
-- src:9830 | material was with B’s consent and the material depicts B only, A and B
-- src:9831 | only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BN (src:9708-9831)
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BN(1) (src:9710-9722)
@export Whether the defence in section 377BN(1) of the Penal Code 1871 is made out for a charge under section 377BK of possession of or access to child abuse material: the accused proves the possession or access was not intentional and, on becoming aware, all reasonable steps to cease it were taken as soon as practicable
GIVEN `the charge is under section 377BK of having possession of or gaining access to child abuse material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge one under s 377BK of having possession of or gaining access to child abuse material?
      `the accused person did not intentionally come into possession of or gain access to child abuse material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the accused proved that he or she did not intentionally come into possession of or gain access to the material? (s 377BN(1)(a))
      `on becoming aware, as soon as it was practicable to do so, the accused person took all reasonable steps in the circumstances to cease possession of or access to the material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the accused proved that, on becoming aware, as soon as it was practicable, he or she took all reasonable steps in the circumstances to cease possession of or access to it? (s 377BN(1)(b))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BN(1) the defence of unintended possession or access is made out` MEANS
    IF `the charge is under section 377BK of having possession of or gaining access to child abuse material` AND `the accused person did not intentionally come into possession of or gain access to child abuse material` AND `on becoming aware, as soon as it was practicable to do so, the accused person took all reasonable steps in the circumstances to cease possession of or access to the material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says what the accused can prove to have a defence; it does not say that an accused who cannot prove it has none

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BN(2) (src:9726-9744)
@export Whether the defence in section 377BN(2) of the Penal Code 1871 is made out for a charge under sections 377BH to 377BK: the act was done for the prevention, detection, investigation or punishment of an offence, proceedings, or safety or national security, without intent to cause injury to the person depicted and with reasonable cause, and the material was not kept longer than reasonably necessary
GIVEN `the charge is under sections 377BH to 377BK` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge one under ss 377BH to 377BK?
      `the act was done for the prevention, detection, investigation or punishment of any offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done for the prevention, detection, investigation or punishment of any offence?
      `the act was done for the conduct of contemplated or pending proceedings in any court or tribunal, or to obtain evidence for the purpose of contemplating such proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done for the conduct of contemplated or pending proceedings in any court or tribunal, or to obtain evidence for the purpose of contemplating such proceedings?
      `the act was done for safety or national security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done for safety or national security?
      `the act was done without intent to cause injury to the person depicted in the child abuse material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done without intent to cause injury to the person depicted in the child abuse material?
      `the act was done with reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done with reasonable cause?
      `the child abuse material was not kept for a period longer than what was reasonably necessary or required for the purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the child abuse material not kept for a period longer than what was reasonably necessary or required for those purposes? (s 377BN(2)(b))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BN(2) the defence of a protected purpose is made out` MEANS
    IF `the charge is under sections 377BH to 377BK` AND (`the act was done for the prevention, detection, investigation or punishment of any offence` OR `the act was done for the conduct of contemplated or pending proceedings in any court or tribunal, or to obtain evidence for the purpose of contemplating such proceedings` OR `the act was done for safety or national security`) AND `the act was done without intent to cause injury to the person depicted in the child abuse material` AND `the act was done with reasonable cause` AND `the child abuse material was not kept for a period longer than what was reasonably necessary or required for the purposes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence to a charge for an offence under sections 377BH to 377BK if (a) the act ... was done for any of the following purposes ... and with reasonable cause ...; (b) the child abuse material was not kept for a period longer than ..." (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BN(3) (src:9749-9757)
@export Whether the defence in section 377BN(3) of the Penal Code 1871 is made out for a charge under sections 377BH to 377BK: the act has a legitimate purpose related to science, medicine, education or art, and did not pose an undue risk of harm to any person below 16 years of age
GIVEN `the charge is under sections 377BH to 377BK` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge one under ss 377BH to 377BK?
      `the act has a legitimate purpose related to science, medicine, education or art` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act have a legitimate purpose related to science, medicine, education or art? An act has a legitimate purpose related to art which reasonable persons would regard as art (Explanation)
      `the act did not pose an undue risk of harm to any person below 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act NOT pose an undue risk of harm to any person below 16 years of age?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BN(3) the defence of a legitimate purpose is made out` MEANS
    IF `the charge is under sections 377BH to 377BK` AND `the act has a legitimate purpose related to science, medicine, education or art` AND `the act did not pose an undue risk of harm to any person below 16 years of age`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence to a charge for an offence under sections 377BH to 377BK if the act ... (a) has a legitimate purpose related to science, medicine, education or art; and (b) did not pose an undue risk of harm to any person below 16 years of age" (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BN(3) Explanation (src:9756-9757)
@export Whether an act has a legitimate purpose related to art, section 377BN(3) Explanation of the Penal Code 1871: it has if reasonable persons would regard it as art
GIVEN `reasonable persons would regard the act as art` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would reasonable persons regard the act as art?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BN(3) Explanation the act has a legitimate purpose related to art` MEANS
    IF `reasonable persons would regard the act as art`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An act has a legitimate purpose related to art which reasonable persons would regard as art" (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BN(4) (src:9773-9778)
@export Whether the defence in section 377BN(4) of the Penal Code 1871 is made out for a charge under sections 377BH to 377BK: the accused is below 16 years of age and the child abuse material is an image of the accused alone
GIVEN `the charge is under sections 377BH to 377BK` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge one under ss 377BH to 377BK?
      `the accused person is below 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused person below 16 years of age? Set from the helper `below 16 years of age` on the accused's age
      `the child abuse material is an image of the accused person alone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child abuse material an image of the accused person alone?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BN(4) the defence of the child's own image is made out` MEANS
    IF `the charge is under sections 377BH to 377BK` AND `the accused person is below 16 years of age` AND `the child abuse material is an image of the accused person alone`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence to a charge for an offence under sections 377BH to 377BK if (a) the accused person (A) is below 16 years of age; and (b) the child abuse material that is alleged to constitute the offence is an image of A alone" (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BN(5) (src:9788-9793)
@export Whether it is a defence to a charge relating to child abuse material or abusive material under sections 377BG to 377BL that the accused honestly and reasonably, but mistakenly, believed that reasonable persons would not regard the material as offensive, section 377BN(5) of the Penal Code 1871: it is not
GIVEN `the accused mistakenly but honestly and reasonably believed that reasonable persons would not regard the material as offensive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused hold a mistaken but honest and reasonable belief that reasonable persons would not regard the material as being, in the circumstances, offensive? The answer changes nothing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BN(5) a mistaken belief that the material is not offensive is a defence` MEANS
    JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not a defence to a charge for an offence relating to child abuse material or abusive material (as the case may be) under sections 377BG to 377BL that, at the time of the conduct constituting the offence, the accused was under a mistaken but honest and reasonable belief that reasonable persons would not regard the child abuse material or abusive material ... as being, in the circumstances, offensive"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BN(6)(a) (src:9798-9809)
@export Whether the defence in section 377BN(6)(a) of the Penal Code 1871 is made out for a charge under section 377BG(1) or 377BH(1) where the offender and the person below 16 years of age are married: the material involves only A and B in its production, depicts B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16, and was produced with B's consent
GIVEN `the charge is under section 377BG(1) or 377BH(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge one under s 377BG(1) or 377BH(1)?
      `A and B are married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the offender (A) and the person below 16 years of age (B) married?
      `the child abuse material involves only A and B in its production` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the child abuse material involve only A and B in its production?
      `the child abuse material depicts B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the child abuse material depict B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age?
      `the child abuse material was produced with B's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the child abuse material produced with B's consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BN(6)(a) the defence of marriage to a charge under section 377BG(1) or 377BH(1) is made out` MEANS
    IF `the charge is under section 377BG(1) or 377BH(1)` AND `A and B are married` AND `the child abuse material involves only A and B in its production` AND `the child abuse material depicts B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age` AND `the child abuse material was produced with B's consent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence to a charge for the following offences in circumstances where the offender (A) and the person below 16 years of age (B) are married and subject to the following respective conditions: (a) an offence under section 377BG(1) or 377BH(1) if the child abuse material (i) involves only A and B in its production; (ii) depicts B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age; and (iii) was produced with B's consent" (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BN(6)(b) (src:9811-9820)
@export Whether the defence in section 377BN(6)(b) of the Penal Code 1871 is made out for a charge under section 377BI where the offender and the person below 16 years of age are married: the distribution occurs between A and B only, involves material depicting B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16, and was with B's consent
GIVEN `the charge is under section 377BI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge one under s 377BI?
      `A and B are married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the offender (A) and the person below 16 years of age (B) married?
      `the distribution occurs between A and B only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the distribution occur between A and B only?
      `the material depicts B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material depict B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age?
      `the distribution was with B's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the distribution with B's consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BN(6)(b) the defence of marriage to a charge under section 377BI is made out` MEANS
    IF `the charge is under section 377BI` AND `A and B are married` AND `the distribution occurs between A and B only` AND `the material depicts B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age` AND `the distribution was with B's consent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) an offence under section 377BI if the distribution of the child abuse material (i) occurs between A and B only; (ii) involves material depicting B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age; and (iii) was distributed with B's consent" (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BN(6)(c) (src:9822-9827)
@export Whether the defence in section 377BN(6)(c) of the Penal Code 1871 is made out for a charge under section 377BJ(2) where the offender and the person below 16 years of age are married: the offer occurs between A and B only and involves material depicting B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16
GIVEN `the charge is under section 377BJ(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge one under s 377BJ(2)?
      `A and B are married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the offender (A) and the person below 16 years of age (B) married?
      `the offer to acquire, buy or gain access to the child abuse material occurs between A and B only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offer to acquire, buy or gain access to the child abuse material occur between A and B only?
      `the material depicts B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material depict B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BN(6)(c) the defence of marriage to a charge under section 377BJ(2) is made out` MEANS
    IF `the charge is under section 377BJ(2)` AND `A and B are married` AND `the offer to acquire, buy or gain access to the child abuse material occurs between A and B only` AND `the material depicts B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) an offence under section 377BJ(2) if the offer to acquire, buy, or gain access to the child abuse material (i) occurs between A and B only; and (ii) involves material depicting B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age" (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BN(6)(d) (src:9829-9831)
@export Whether the defence in section 377BN(6)(d) of the Penal Code 1871 is made out for a charge under section 377BK(1) where the offender and the person below 16 years of age are married: the possession was with B's consent and the material depicts B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16
GIVEN `the charge is under section 377BK(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge one under s 377BK(1)?
      `A and B are married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the offender (A) and the person below 16 years of age (B) married?
      `the possession of the child abuse material was with B's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the possession of the child abuse material with B's consent?
      `the material depicts B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material depict B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377BN(6)(d) the defence of marriage to a charge under section 377BK(1) is made out` MEANS
    IF `the charge is under section 377BK(1)` AND `A and B are married` AND `the possession of the child abuse material was with B's consent` AND `the material depicts B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) an offence under section 377BK(1) if the possession of the child abuse material was with B's consent and the material depicts B only, A and B only, or A only if A is below 16 years of age" (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)



§§ `s 377BO - child abuse material offences outside or partially outside Singapore`

-- src:9835 | Child abuse material offences outside or partially outside Singapore
-- src:9837 | 377BO.—(1) Any person, being a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore, who
-- src:9838 | does, outside Singapore, any act that would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence
-- src:9839 | under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3), shall be guilty of an offence under
-- src:9840 | section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3), as the case may be.
-- src:9844 | (2) To avoid doubt, any person (A) who does in Singapore, any act involving a person
-- src:9845 | below 16 years of age (B) and B is outside Singapore, that would if B were in Singapore
-- src:9846 | constitute an offence under section 377BG or 377BH, shall be guilty of an offence under
-- src:9847 | section 377BG or 377BH, as the case may be.
-- src:9851 | (3) Any person who does outside Singapore, any act involving a person below
-- src:9852 | 16 years of age (B) and B is in Singapore, that would if done in Singapore constitute an
-- src:9853 | offence under section 377BG or 377BH, shall be guilty of an offence under
-- src:9854 | section 377BG or 377BH, as the case may be.
-- src:9858 | (4) Subsections (5) and (6) apply only where A is in a relationship that is exploitative
-- src:9859 | of B.
-- src:9863 | (5) To avoid doubt, any person (A) who does in Singapore, any act involving a person
-- src:9866 | who is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age (B) and B is outside Singapore, that
-- src:9867 | would if B were in Singapore constitute an offence under section 377BL(2) or (3), shall
-- src:9868 | be guilty of an offence under section 377BL(2) or (3), as the case may be.
-- src:9872 | (6) Any person (A) who does outside Singapore, any act involving a person who is of
-- src:9873 | or above 16 but below 18 years of age (B) and B is in Singapore, that would if done in
-- src:9874 | Singapore constitute an offence under section 377BL(2) or (3), shall be guilty of an
-- src:9875 | offence under section 377BL(2) or (3), as the case may be.
-- src:9879 | (7) To avoid doubt, any person who does in Singapore an act which is a physical
-- src:9880 | element of an offence under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3) shall be guilty of
-- src:9881 | an offence under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3), as the case may be, if all
-- src:9882 | the fault elements and physical elements of the offence are proven even though other
-- src:9883 | physical elements of the same offence occurred outside Singapore.
-- src:9885 | Illustrations
-- src:9887 | (a) A, a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore, films in a foreign country a video recording of
-- src:9888 | child abuse material involving a person below 16 years of age (B). B is in that foreign country during
-- src:9889 | the filming. A is guilty of an offence under section 377BG or 377BH read with section 377BO(1).
-- src:9891 | (b) A, who is in Singapore, uses remote video facilities to film a video recording of child abuse
-- src:9892 | material involving a person below 16 years of age (B). B is in a foreign country during the filming. A is
-- src:9893 | guilty of an offence under section 377BG or 377BH read with section 377BO(2).
-- src:9895 | (c) A, who is in a foreign country and is not a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore, uses
-- src:9896 | remote video facilities to film a video recording of child abuse material involving a person below 16
-- src:9897 | years of age (B). B is in Singapore during the filming. A is guilty of an offence under section 377BG or
-- src:9898 | 377BH read with section 377BO(3).
-- src:9900 | (d) A, who is in Singapore, uses computer software to alter and reproduce child abuse material
-- src:9901 | which was not filmed in Singapore. The child abuse material is not stored in Singapore but in a
-- src:9902 | computer server in a foreign country which A accesses through A’s computer in Singapore. A is guilty of
-- src:9903 | an offence under section 377BH read with section 377BO(7).

-- 377BO is read as six limbs, (1), (2), (3), (5), (6) and (7); (4) only makes (5) and (6) turn on the exploitative
-- relationship. The offence is "an offence under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3), as the case may be":
-- the underlying offence is a nested record for the same act, and a charge is framed under the underlying section
-- read with the limb of 377BO (FORK DEF-B7). Where the facts make out more than one underlying offence, the charge
-- is framed under the first in the order the text names them: 377BG, 377BH, 377BL(2), 377BL(3).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BO (src:9835-9903)
DECLARE `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person involved in the act (B), or a description of the material, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by filming B in a sexual pose on a visit to Batam"
    `the accused is a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore? (s 377BO(1))
    `the accused does the act outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the accused do the act outside Singapore? (s 377BO(1), (3), (6))
    `the accused does the act in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the accused do the act in Singapore? (s 377BO(2), (5))
    `the act involves a person below 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act involve a person (B) below 16 years of age? (s 377BO(2), (3))
    `the act involves a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act involve a person (B) of or above 16 but below 18 years of age? (s 377BO(5), (6))
    `B is outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B outside Singapore? (s 377BO(2), (5))
    `B is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B in Singapore? (s 377BO(3), (6))
    `A is in a relationship that is exploitative of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused (A) in a relationship that is exploitative of B? Subsections (5) and (6) apply only where this is so (s 377BO(4))
    `the accused does in Singapore an act which is a physical element of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the accused do in Singapore an act which is a physical element of an offence under s 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3), the other physical elements having occurred outside Singapore? (s 377BO(7))
    `the act as an offence under section 377BG` IS A `Child Abuse Material Use Facts` @desc The facts of the same act read as if done in Singapore, under s 377BG
    `the act as an offence under section 377BH` IS A `Child Abuse Material Production Facts` @desc The facts of the same act read as if done in Singapore, under s 377BH
    `the act as an offence under section 377BL` IS A `Exploitative Abusive Material Facts` @desc The facts of the same act read as if done in Singapore, under s 377BL(2) or (3)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BO (src:9837-9883)
@export Whether the act is one that would constitute an offence under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3) of the Penal Code 1871 if done in Singapore, for section 377BO
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts` @desc The nested facts of the same act under ss 377BG, 377BH and 377BL
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act would constitute an offence under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3)` f IF
        `offence under s 377BG(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BG`)
    OR  `offence under s 377BH(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BH`)
    OR  `offence under s 377BL(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BL`)
    OR  `offence under s 377BL(3)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BL`)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BO(1) (src:9837-9840)
@export Whether the accused is guilty under section 377BO(1) of the Penal Code 1871: a citizen or permanent resident who does outside Singapore an act that would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts` @desc The geography, and the nested facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is guilty under section 377BO(1)` f IF
        "Any person, being a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore, who does, outside Singapore, any act that would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3)"
   ...  f's `the accused is a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore`
   ...  f's `the accused does the act outside Singapore`
   ...  `the act would constitute an offence under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3)` f

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BO(2) (src:9844-9847)
@export Whether the accused is guilty under section 377BO(2) of the Penal Code 1871: a person who does in Singapore an act involving a person below 16 years of age who is outside Singapore, that would if B were in Singapore constitute an offence under section 377BG or 377BH
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts` @desc The geography, and the nested facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is guilty under section 377BO(2)` f IF
        "any person (A) who does in Singapore, any act involving a person below 16 years of age (B) and B is outside Singapore"
   ...  f's `the accused does the act in Singapore`
   ...  f's `the act involves a person below 16 years of age`
   ...  f's `B is outside Singapore`
   ...  "that would if B were in Singapore constitute an offence under section 377BG or 377BH"
   ...  (    `offence under s 377BG(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BG`)
        OR   `offence under s 377BH(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BH`) )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BO(3) (src:9851-9854)
@export Whether the accused is guilty under section 377BO(3) of the Penal Code 1871: a person who does outside Singapore an act involving a person below 16 years of age who is in Singapore, that would if done in Singapore constitute an offence under section 377BG or 377BH
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts` @desc The geography, and the nested facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is guilty under section 377BO(3)` f IF
        "Any person who does outside Singapore, any act involving a person below 16 years of age (B) and B is in Singapore"
   ...  f's `the accused does the act outside Singapore`
   ...  f's `the act involves a person below 16 years of age`
   ...  f's `B is in Singapore`
   ...  "that would if done in Singapore constitute an offence under section 377BG or 377BH"
   ...  (    `offence under s 377BG(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BG`)
        OR   `offence under s 377BH(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BH`) )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BO(5) (src:9858-9868)
@export Whether the accused is guilty under section 377BO(5) of the Penal Code 1871: in an exploitative relationship, a person who does in Singapore an act involving a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age who is outside Singapore, that would if B were in Singapore constitute an offence under section 377BL(2) or (3)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts` @desc The geography, and the nested facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is guilty under section 377BO(5)` f IF
        "(4) Subsections (5) and (6) apply only where A is in a relationship that is exploitative of B"
   ...  f's `A is in a relationship that is exploitative of B`
   ...  "(5) any person (A) who does in Singapore, any act involving a person who is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age (B) and B is outside Singapore"
   ...  f's `the accused does the act in Singapore`
   ...  f's `the act involves a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`
   ...  f's `B is outside Singapore`
   ...  "that would if B were in Singapore constitute an offence under section 377BL(2) or (3)"
   ...  (    `offence under s 377BL(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BL`)
        OR   `offence under s 377BL(3)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BL`) )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BO(6) (src:9872-9875)
@export Whether the accused is guilty under section 377BO(6) of the Penal Code 1871: in an exploitative relationship, a person who does outside Singapore an act involving a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age who is in Singapore, that would if done in Singapore constitute an offence under section 377BL(2) or (3)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts` @desc The geography, and the nested facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is guilty under section 377BO(6)` f IF
        "(4) Subsections (5) and (6) apply only where A is in a relationship that is exploitative of B"
   ...  f's `A is in a relationship that is exploitative of B`
   ...  "(6) Any person (A) who does outside Singapore, any act involving a person who is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age (B) and B is in Singapore"
   ...  f's `the accused does the act outside Singapore`
   ...  f's `the act involves a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`
   ...  f's `B is in Singapore`
   ...  "that would if done in Singapore constitute an offence under section 377BL(2) or (3)"
   ...  (    `offence under s 377BL(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BL`)
        OR   `offence under s 377BL(3)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BL`) )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BO(7) (src:9879-9883)
@export Whether the accused is guilty under section 377BO(7) of the Penal Code 1871: a person who does in Singapore an act which is a physical element of an offence under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3), if all the fault and physical elements are proven even though other physical elements occurred outside Singapore
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts` @desc The geography, and the nested facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is guilty under section 377BO(7)` f IF
        "any person who does in Singapore an act which is a physical element of an offence under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3)"
   ...  f's `the accused does in Singapore an act which is a physical element of the offence`
   ...  "if all the fault elements and physical elements of the offence are proven even though other physical elements of the same offence occurred outside Singapore"
   ...  `the act would constitute an offence under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3)` f

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BO (src:9837-9883)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3) of the Penal Code 1871 by section 377BO (acts outside or partly outside Singapore)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts` @desc The geography, and the nested facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 377BO` f IF
        `is guilty under section 377BO(1)` f
    OR  `is guilty under section 377BO(2)` f
    OR  `is guilty under section 377BO(3)` f
    OR  `is guilty under section 377BO(5)` f
    OR  `is guilty under section 377BO(6)` f
    OR  `is guilty under section 377BO(7)` f

-- The limb that applies, for the "read with" of the charge; the first in the order (1), (2), (3), (5), (6), (7).
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the limb of section 377BO that applies` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `is guilty under section 377BO(1)` f THEN "377BO(1)"
        IF `is guilty under section 377BO(2)` f THEN "377BO(2)"
        IF `is guilty under section 377BO(3)` f THEN "377BO(3)"
        IF `is guilty under section 377BO(5)` f THEN "377BO(5)"
        IF `is guilty under section 377BO(6)` f THEN "377BO(6)"
        OTHERWISE "377BO(7)"

-- The underlying section, in the order the text names them.
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the underlying section of section 377BO` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `offence under s 377BG(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BG`) THEN "377BG"
        IF `offence under s 377BH(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BH`) THEN "377BH"
        IF `offence under s 377BL(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BL`) THEN "377BL(2)"
        OTHERWISE "377BL(3)"

GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the punishment words of the underlying section of section 377BO` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `offence under s 377BG(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BG`) THEN `punishment prescribed by s 377BG(2)`'s words
        IF `offence under s 377BH(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BH`) THEN `punishment prescribed by s 377BH(2)`'s words
        IF `offence under s 377BL(2)` (f's `the act as an offence under section 377BL`) THEN `punishment prescribed by s 377BL(2)`'s words
        OTHERWISE `punishment prescribed by s 377BL(3)`'s words

GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the opening of the body of a charge read with section 377BO` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `is guilty under section 377BO(1)` f THEN "being a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore, did outside Singapore an act which would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section "
        IF `is guilty under section 377BO(2)` f THEN "did in Singapore an act involving a person below 16 years of age who was outside Singapore, which would, if the person had been in Singapore, constitute an offence under section "
        IF `is guilty under section 377BO(3)` f THEN "did outside Singapore an act involving a person below 16 years of age who was in Singapore, which would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section "
        IF `is guilty under section 377BO(5)` f THEN "being in a relationship that is exploitative of the person, did in Singapore an act involving a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age who was outside Singapore, which would, if the person had been in Singapore, constitute an offence under section "
        IF `is guilty under section 377BO(6)` f THEN "being in a relationship that is exploitative of the person, did outside Singapore an act involving a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age who was in Singapore, which would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section "
        OTHERWISE "did in Singapore an act which is a physical element of an offence under section "

GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of the offence read with section 377BO not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (`the act would constitute an offence under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3)` f) "the act would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3)"),
        (`missing unless` (`is guilty under section 377BO(1)` f OR `is guilty under section 377BO(2)` f OR `is guilty under section 377BO(3)` f OR `is guilty under section 377BO(5)` f OR `is guilty under section 377BO(6)` f OR `is guilty under section 377BO(7)` f) "a limb of section 377BO applies: a citizen or permanent resident acting outside Singapore; acting in Singapore involving a person below 16 who is outside it; acting outside Singapore involving a person below 16 who is in it; the same for a person of or above 16 but below 18 where A is in an exploitative relationship; or an act in Singapore that is a physical element"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 377BO` f) "the elements of section 377BO taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BO (src:9837-9883)
@export Frame a charge under section 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3) of the Penal Code 1871 read with section 377BO (an act outside or partly outside Singapore), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts` @desc The geography, the nested facts, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 377BO` f MEANS
    `frame the charge read with` (f's particulars) (`the underlying section of section 377BO` f) (LIST (`the limb of section 377BO that applies` f)) "child abuse material offence outside or partially outside Singapore"
        (`the punishment words of the underlying section of section 377BO` f)
        (`offence under s 377BO` f)
        (CONCAT (`the opening of the body of a charge read with section 377BO` f), (`the underlying section of section 377BO` f), " of the Penal Code 1871, involving ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of the offence read with section 377BO not made out` f)

